hadiths[683]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, was asked about such water that is in a desert and in which beasts and animals come to drink, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water is clean"
"2","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates from his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was informed about water from which animals and beasts come to drink, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When the water is two-fold"
"3","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates to his father, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water from which beasts and animals drink, so he said: \When the water is two cups"
"4","This tradition is narrated from some other traditions."
"5","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the following statement from his father (sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar radi Allahu anhuma): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about a water from which animals and beasts drink. One tradition has these words: beasts and beasts. So the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water is two-fold"
"6","The same hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but it has these words: animals and beasts (meaning the word animal is transmitted first)."
"7","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water is two cups"
"8","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about such water (from which animals and beasts drink), and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When water is divided into two parts"
"9","This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"10","This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"11","This tradition along with other evidences has been narrated by Abdullah bin Abdullah on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) from the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"12","Narrated by Abdullah bin Umar: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water from which beasts and animals drink. The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"
"13","Abdullah bin Abdullah narrates the same from his father (sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him) from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"14","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Abdullah, his father (on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him)."
"15","Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates this statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about such water (from which animals and beasts drink), and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When the water becomes two cups"
"16","Ubaidullah narrates this on the authority of Abdullah bin Umar, who said: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, being asked about water that is in a deserted place and animals and beasts drink from it, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two folds"
"17","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: I heard the Holy Prophet (PBUH) saying this: A person asked him about such water, which is in a deserted place, from which animals and beasts drink, then the Prophet (PBUH) said: \When the water is divided"
"18","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"19","The same tradition is narrated from another hadith."
"20","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrates this about the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He was asked about a well into which dead bodies are put, and from which dogs and other animals drink water. The same hadith is narrated on the authority of Ubaidullah bin Abdullah (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him) along with another chain of transmission."
"21","The same hadith along with some other traditions is narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdullah (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar). However, some narrators have also quoted it as a \suspended\"" tradition."""
"22","Asim bin Munzar narrates: I entered a garden with Ubaidullah bin Abdullah, in which there was a pool of water with the skin of a dead camel lying on it, so Ubaydullah bin Abdullah performed ablution on it. The skin of a dead camel is lying inside it, so he told me this statement of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, regarding his father."
"23","This hadith is transmitted along with another chain of transmission, but in this chain of transmission, the words \the narrator is in doubt"
"24","Abd al-Jabar al-Makki and Musa ibn Ismail and Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Aishah narrated this chain of narration on the authority of Hamad ibn Salama and they said in it: If the water is two qala, it is not najis. They did not say \or three\""."""
"25","Asim bin Munzar narrates: We were in a garden. The narrator has doubts. These words are: He was ours or perhaps these words were Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abdullah's. Meanwhile, when it was time for prayer, Abdullah got up, and went to the tank in the garden and started performing ablution from it. Although the skin of a camel was lying in this tank, I said: You are performing ablution with it, if it has skin. He said: My father narrated this hadith to me regarding the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him. The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two cups"
"26","The judge Al-Ḥusayn ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us; Al-Ḥasan ibn Muḥammad al-Zaʿfarānī narrated to us; Yaʿqūb ibn Isḥāq narrated to us; Ḥammād ibn Salamah narrated to us. And Abū Bakr al-Shāfiʿī narrated to us; Bishr ibn Mūsā narrated to us. And Daʿlaj ibn Aḥmad narrated to us; Ibrāhīm ibn Ṣāliḥ al-Shīrāzī narrated to us; they both said: Al-Ḥumaydī narrated to us; he said: Bishr ibn al-Sarī and Al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Jabbār narrated to us, from Ḥammād ibn Salamah, from ʿĀṣim ibn al-Mundhir, with this chain of transmission, similar to the statement of ʿAffān: ""When the water amounts to two qullahs, it does not become impure."""
"27","The same tradition is also narrated along with another document, which has these words: \When water becomes two-fold"
"28","Ubaidullah bin Abdullah narrates this on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"
"29","This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Umar, the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: \When the water becomes two-fold"
"30","This same tradition along with another chain of transmission is related to Mujahid from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (Radi Allahu Anhu) as a “Mowquf” Hadith."
"31","Asim says: The word \al-Qalal\"" used in the text of hadiths refers to \""big pots\""."""
"32","Yahya bin Aqeel narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When water becomes two-fold"
"33","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When I was raised from the seventh heaven towards the Sadrat al-Muntahi, its fruits were as large as the fruits of the Hijr, and its leaves were like the ears of an elephant. What is it? So they said: The inner rivers are in Paradise and the outer rivers are the Nile and the Euphrates.\""34"""
"34","Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Salih al-Kufi narrated to us: ‘Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Harun al-Baladi narrated to us: Isma‘il ibn al-Hasan al-Harrani narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn ‘Ulwan narrated to us from Nafi‘, from Ibn ‘Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out on one of his journeys and traveled by night. They passed by a man sitting by his watering trough. ‘Umar said: “O owner of the trough, did wild beasts drink from your trough tonight?” The Prophet (ﷺ) said to him: “O owner of the trough, do not inform him; this is a drinking place for them. They have what they carried in their bellies, and for us remains a drink that is pure and purifying.”"
"35","This hadith is also narrated along with another document."
"36","Wakiyya says: The learned note everything, whether it is in their favor or not, and the heretics only note that which is in their favor."
"37","Yahya bin Abu Zaida says: It is better to note the hadith than not to note it."
"38","Sayyiduna Jabir Ibn Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When the water reaches the limit of forty Qala"
"39","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Amr Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \When the water becomes 40 galahs"
"40","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (RA) says: \When the water is forty qala"
"41","This same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Amr (RA)."
"42","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Amr Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: \When the water becomes forty qala"
"43","Muhammad bin Mankader narrates: When the water is 40 feet deep, it is not impure, or perhaps a word similar to this has been described by him."
"44","Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Hurairah narrates this saying of his father (Sayyidna Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him), he says: \When the water reaches the amount of forty Qala"
"45","Sayyiduna Thawban Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Water is a purifying thing"
"46","Sayyidna Rashid bin Saad Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Nothing defiles water"
"47","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \Nothing defiles water"
"48","Sayyiduna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Nothing defiles water.\"""""
"49","Rashid bin Saad narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Nothing defiles water except that which overpowers its smell or taste.\"" This hadith is \""musal\"" and a narrator named Abu Usama transmitted it to Rashid bin Sa'd as a \""mawquf\"" hadith."""
"50","Abu Awun Rashid bin Sa'd states: Nothing defiles water, except that which changes the smell or taste of the water."
"51","Saeed bin Musayyib says: Water is pure, nothing impures it."
"52","Dawood bin Abu Hind narrates: We asked Saeed bin Musaib about a well and a reservoir from which even dogs drink, so he said: Water has been revealed as a pure thing, nothing defiles it."
"53","Dawood quotes the statement of Saeed bin Musaib: \Allah has revealed water as a pure thing"
"54","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said: O Messenger of Allah! We perform ablution from the \Baa'a\"" well"
"55","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: I heard from the Prophet (PBUH), when he was asked: O Messenger of Allah! We drink water from the well of \Baa'ah\"""
"56","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about these reservoirs, which come at different places on the way to Makkah and Medina. He was told: Dogs and beasts drink water from these reservoirs. The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whatever they put in their stomachs is their air"
"57","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said to the Prophet (PBUH): Water is brought for you from a well called \Baa'ah\"""
"58","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him."
"59","Sayyidna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (RA) narrates: It was said to the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! Shall we perform ablution from a well called Baa'a? In which the clothes of menstruating women, the meat of dogs and dirt are put, then the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Water is pure and nothing impures it.\"""""
"60","This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Saeed Khudri (RA)."
"61","Sayyidna Sahl bin Saad Sa'idi (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) drank the water of the \Baa'a\"" well."""
"62","Abu Sa'eed and Yahya bin Abd al-Rahman narrate: Once Sayyiduna Umar, may God be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Amr ibn al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, passed by a reservoir, and Sayyidna Amr, may God be pleased with him, inquired: O owner of the tank! Do the beasts also come and drink water at this reservoir of yours? So Sayyiduna Umar Radiyallahu Anhu said: \O owner of the reservoir! Do not tell us about this (because to drink water from such a reservoir) sometimes we come after the beasts and sometimes they come after us.\"""""
"63","Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: When we were in Syria, I brought water to the service of Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab, he performed ablution with this water and then inquired: Where did you bring this water from? I have never seen any heavenly water sweeter and purer than this. Narrator narrates: I said: I have brought it from the house of an old Christian woman. When Sayyiduna Umar (RA) performed ablution, he came to her. He said: \O old woman! Accept Islam"
"64","Zayd bin Aslam narrates this statement of his father: Sayyiduna Umar performed ablution at the house of a Christian, then he went to this woman, he said: \O big sister! Accept Islam"
"65","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: Once an Abyssinian fell into the well of Zamzam, i.e. he fell down and died, his body was taken out under the order of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) and about the well, Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) instructed that it be cleaned. The narrator narrates: But the water of the spring did not come under the control of the people, it came from the rock (black stone). Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) instructed about it: It should be completely covered with cloths, until it is completely covered, when people closed it, then water came out of it."
"66","Sayyiduna Abu Tufail narrates: Once a boy fell into the well of Zam Zam and all the water was taken out of him."
"67","Ibrahim Nakhai says: Every living thing whose blood is flowing (if it falls into a well), then ablution will not be performed with the water of that well. Shuba says: I think, he also mentioned the chameleon."
"68","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is purifying.\"""""
"69","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said this about the sea: \Its water is purifying and its dead is lawful.\"""""
"70","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the sea and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead matter is lawful.\"" These words of the hadith are narrated from a narrator named Fazl Bin Ziyad"
"71","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about the water of the sea, and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
"72","Abu Tufail narrates: Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (RA) was asked about the water of the sea, and he said: \Its water is purifying and its dead matter is lawful.\"""""
"73","On the authority of Imam Muhammad Baqir (may Allah be pleased with him) (Imam Zain al-Abidin may Allah be pleased with him) on the authority of his father (Imam Hussain (may Allah be pleased with him)) on the authority of Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrate this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the water of the sea, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.”"
"74","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""
"75","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about sea water: \Its dead body is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""
"76","This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him, on the authority of Sayyiduna Anas."
"77","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about sea water and he said: \Sea water is pure.\"" The narrators have narrated it in the same way"
"78","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \He who cannot be purified by the water of the sea"
"79","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once this was mentioned to me, some people after bathing in the Sea of Khadr say: It is obligatory on us, we should also bathe with other water (Sayyidna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) \He who is not purified by the water of the sea"
"80","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: A person asked the Prophet (PBUH): O Messenger of Allah! We people travel in the sea and take a little water with us. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
"81","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about performing ablution with sea water, and the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
"82","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about sea water: Should it be used for ablution? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Its water is pure and its dead body is lawful.\"""""
"83","Amr ibn Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \The dead body of the sea is lawful and its water is pure.\"""""
"84","Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (RA) narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \O Salman! Any food or drink in which an animal (i.e. worm"
"85","Aslam, a freed slave of Sayyiduna Umar (RA) narrates: Water was heated in a pot for Sayyidna Umar (RA), and he used to bathe in it. The chain of this hadith is \Sahih\""."""
"86","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me, while I was heating some water in the sun, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \O girl! Do not do this"
"87","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade performing ablution with water that has been kept in the sun, or bathing with it. The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \It may result in rain.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Umar bin Muhammad Asim. No one else has narrated this tradition from Falih"
"88","Hasan bin Azhar narrates: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) has said this: \Do not bathe with water heated in the sun"
"89","Hadith 85: It is narrated about Sayyidah Umm Hani (may Allah be pleased with her) that: She has declared it abominable to perform ablution with water in which bread has been soaked."
"90","Zayd bin Aslam narrates: (God's guidance is:) \When you stand for prayer"
"91","Imam Malik bin Anas has quoted Zayd bin Aslam's saying about this saying of Allah Almighty: \O you who believe! When you stand for prayer.\"" Zayd bin Aslam narrates: This means: When you wake up from sleep (do ablution)."""
"92","Qays narrates this about Sayyiduna Jarir (bin Abdullah Bijli): He used to instruct his household to perform ablution with water in which miswak was placed."
"93","Qays narrates: Sayyiduna Jarir (bin Abdullah Al-Bijli, may God be pleased with him) used to instruct his family: Do ablution with the water in which I kept the miswak. Its certificate is \Correct\""."""
"94","Sayyidna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to use the water left over from ablution to rub his face."
"95","Sayyiduna Anas Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to use the water left over from his ablution to rub his face."
"96","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever drinks something from a gold or silver vessel"
"97","Abu Burda narrated: Once I and my father (Sayyidna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him) attended the service of Sayyidna Ali bin Abu Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, and Sayyidna Ali, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to us: \The Holy Prophet"
"98","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a dead goat, he said: \Why don't you use its skin?\"" People said: O Messenger of Allah! Is it dead? The Prophet"
"99","This tradition is also narrated along with another document, however, the narrator named Aqeel has quoted these additional words in his tradition: \The Prophet"
"100","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a dead goat, he inquired: \Whose does it belong to?\"" People have said: It was given as a charity to the maidservant of Sayyida Maimunah"
"101","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by the pet goat of one of his wives who had died. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Why don't you use its skin?\"" People said: O Messenger of Allah! It is carrion"
"102","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \Its meat is forbidden"
"103","This tradition is narrated from Zuhri along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Its meat has been forbidden to you and its skin (to be used) has been permitted.\"" The chain of this hadith is \""Sahih\""."""
"104","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to the owner of a dead goat: \Why did you not skin it? You used to tan it and get profit from it.\"""""
"105","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the pet goat of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) died, the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Why don't you people use its skin"
"106","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \The way to purify a dead body is this: it should be tanned.\"" Ibrahim Nakhai narrates: The disciples of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) used to say: \""The way to purify wool is this: wash it.\"""""
"107","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: \To tan it is to purify it.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
"108","Aaliyah bint Sabi narrates, Ms. Sayyida Maimunah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told her, once the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by some people of Quraish, who were pulling their sheep like a (dead) donkey is pulled. The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said to them: \If you get his skin (it will be appropriate).\"" They said: It is dead. The Prophet"
"109","Sayyiduna Salama bin Muhibq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the occasion of the Battle of Tabuk, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked a woman for water, and she said: The water I have is in a bottle that belongs to a dead (animal). The woman said: Yes! The Prophet, peace be upon him, said: \As a result of tanning"
"110","The same hadith is also narrated along with another authority, but it contains these words: \By tanning leather"
"111","The same tradition is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \It is its tanning that purifies it.\"""""
"112","The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \His tanning purifies him.\"""""
"113","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Every skin is purified by tanning.\"""""
"114","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When the leather is tanned"
"115","We were informed by Muhammad ibn Makhlad; we were informed by Al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim; Shababah ibn Sawwar narrated to us; Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us. And Abu Bakr al-Azraq, Yusuf ibn Ya'qub ibn Ishaq ibn Buhlul, narrated to us; my grandfather narrated to us; Ammar ibn Salam Abu Muhammad narrated to us; Zafir narrated to us; from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali; from Al-Zuhri; from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah; from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, Mighty and Majestic: ""Say: I do not find in what has been revealed to me anything forbidden to an eater who eats it"" (Surah Al-An'am, verse 145). He said: ""The 'eater' (al-ta'im) is the one who eats. As for the tooth, the horn, the bone, the wool, the hair, the fur, and the sinew—there is no harm in them because they can be washed."" And Shababah said: ""Only that which is eaten of the dead animal (maytah) is forbidden, and that is the flesh. As for the skin, the tooth, the bone, the hair, and the wool—they are lawful."" Abu Bakr al-Hudhali is weak."
"116","Abu Salama bin Abdul Rahman narrates: I heard Ms. Sayyida Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, narrate this: She says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this: \When the skin of a dead body is tanned"
"117","This tradition is narrated by Yusuf bin Safar along with another chain of transmission."
"118","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) declared the meat (eating) of a dead body to be haram, as far as its skin, hair and wool are concerned, there is nothing wrong with it. The narrator of this tradition \Abd al-Jabbar\"" is weak."""
"119","Hazeel bin Shahrabeel narrates the following regarding Sayyida Umm Salama (RA) or Sayyida Zainab (RA) or any other wife of the Prophet (PBUH): When the goat of Sayyida Maimunah (RA) died, the Prophet (PBUH) said to her: \Why don't you people use its skin?\"" Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: O Messenger of Allah! How can we use it"
"120","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him, narrates: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, saying: (Allah the Exalted) said: \Say this! In what has been revealed to me"
"121","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The skin that is tanned becomes pure.\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""
"122","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Tanning the skin of a dead body purifies it.\"""""
"123","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) passed by a goat, he inquired: \What has happened to it?\"" People said: It is dead. The Prophet"
"124","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: \The way to purify leather is this"
"125","Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates: She had a goat which she used to milk. Once the Prophet (PBUH) did not see that goat, so he (PBUH) inquired: \Where is the goat?\"" So the people said: She is dead. The Prophet"
"126","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Use the skin of a dead animal"
"127","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person wakes up from sleep"
"128","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person wakes up from sleep and wants to perform ablution"
"129","Salim bin Abdullah narrates the statement of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a person wakes up from sleep"
"130","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \When a person wakes up from sleep"
"131","Alqamah bin Waqqas narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may God be pleased with him, narrating this. He says: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, say: It will be counted towards the Messenger, and whoever migrated for the sake of this world in order to obtain it or migrated for a woman in order to marry her, his migration will be in the direction towards which he (intentionally) migrated.”"
"132","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \On the Day of Resurrection"
"133","Sayyidna Dahhak bin Qais Fahri (RA) narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Allah Almighty says: \I am free from partners"
"134","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \No one should bathe in stagnant water when he is pregnant.\"" The narrator inquired: O Sayyidna Abu Huraira! Then what should he do? So Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu said: \""Let him get water (and bathe on one side).\"" Its certificate is \""Correct\""."""
"135","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I remember this very well about myself and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We used to perform ablution from the same vessel."
"136","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: I remember well about myself, I used to perform ablution with the same vessel with the Holy Prophet."
"137","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates this statement of Sayyidah Maimunah, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: I was afflicted with janabat, I took a bath with a vessel and some water was left in it, then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought Tashreef. Janabat has not been established. Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a bath with this vessel. In this hadith, the narrator named Samat has been disputed and only the narrator named Sharik has stated this: It is narrated on the authority of Sayyidah Maimunah."
"138","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: In the time of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), men and women (i.e. husband and wife) used to perform ablution from the same vessel. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"139","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to bathe with the water left over from Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with him). Its certificate is \Correct\""."""
"140","Sayyiduna Abdullah ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) used to bathe with the water left over from Sayyida Maimunah (R.A.). Its certificate is \Correct\""."""
"141","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Maimoona bint Harith (RA) told me this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) performed ablution with the water left over from Sayyida Maimoona’s bath. Narrator named Ramadi has narrated this: Sayyida Maimunah (may Allah be pleased with her) performed ablution with water in the state of Janabat, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with water left over from her."
"142","Sayyidna Huqam bin Amr (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) forbade a man to perform ablution with the water left over from a woman's ablution (the narrator has doubts, perhaps these words are:) with the water left after a woman drinks. A narrator named Shuba narrates this: Sulaiman Taymi has narrated this: Abu Hajib has narrated this with reference to a companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has forbidden that a woman should perform ablution with the water left over from her ablution. The name of the narrator named Abu Hajib is Sawada bin Asim, there is a difference in this hadith regarding him, some narrators have quoted it as a “deferred” tradition as a saying of command, it has not been quoted as a “marfu’” tradition until the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him."
"143","Sayyida Khula bint Qays (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: (Sayyida Ayesha (may Allah be pleased with her) says this:) Her hand and the blessed hand of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to enter back and forth in the same vessel."
"144","It is narrated about Sayyidna Salman Farsi, may God be pleased with him: A polytheist mocked him and said to him: I have noted this, your master has taught you everything, even the method of defecation, so Sayyidna Salman Farsi, may God be pleased with him, replied: \Yes! The Messenger of God"
"145","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"146","It is narrated about Sayyidna Salman Farsi (RA): Some polytheists said to him: We have noted this, your master has taught you all kinds of things, even teaching you how to perform abstinence, then Sayyidna Salman Farsi (RA) replied: “Yes! He should perform istanja through or facing the Qiblah, and you have also forbidden us to perform istanja with mengini and bone. The chain of this hadith is \Sahih\""."""
"147","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said this: \When a person goes to defecate"
"148","Narrated Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud: Once the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, went to meet his needs. Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) brought two stones and a ring, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) threw the ring and said: \This is dirt"
"149","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, forbade us to perform abstinence through bone, manganese or coal. The source of this tradition is Syrian and is not authentic."
"150","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to perform ablution with rotten bone, manganese or coal. The narrator of this tradition, Ali bin Rabah, has not been proven to have heard it from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud."
"151","Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman, a companion of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, who was an Ansari, narrates this, he has stated this regarding the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, forbade: \One should perform istanja through bone"
"152","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this, \to cast iron or bone.\"" You have said this: \""These two things do not purify.\"" The authenticity of this tradition is \""Sahih\""."""
"153","Abi ibn Abbas, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather Sayyiduna Sahl ibn Sa'd, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, was asked about the method of ablution, and he said: \Don't you find three stones? Two stones (to clean the sides of the exit) and one stone to (clean the exit).\"" Its certificate is \""Hasan\""."""
"154","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once Saraqa bin Malik Mudalji passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the method of ablution. He should do istanja, which does not involve any Mangani, or do it through three pieces of wood or through three lumps of clay.”"
"155","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person needs to defecate"
"156","Salama bin Wahram narrates: I heard Taaws narrate this: Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrated: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: “When a person starts defecating, he should respect the Qibla of Allah and not turn his back towards it, then purify himself with three stones or with three pieces of wood or with a handful of clay three times. Do it and then recite: All praise is due to Allah, the Exalted, Who has removed from me that which could have tormented me and left within me that which is beneficial to me.\""157"""
"157","Abu Sahl ibn Ziyad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ishaq al-Harbi narrated to us: Harun ibn Ma‘ruf narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Zam‘ah ibn Salih narrated to us from Salamah ibn Wahram and Ibn Tawus, from Tawus, from the Prophet (ﷺ) with this [hadith], mursal."
"158","The same tradition is narrated by Taos along with another chain of transmission."
"159","The same hadith is narrated by Taus along with another chain of transmission and it is narrated as his saying, he has not quoted this tradition as a \marfu'\"" hadith. A narrator named Ali narrates: I inquired from Sufyan: Has a narrator named Zamaa transmitted this tradition as a \""marfu'\"" hadith? So they answered: \""Yes!\"" Then I asked Salama about this"
"160","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Maswak has ten virtues: it is a cause of God's pleasure"
"161","Marwan Asfar narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him, he made his camel sit facing the Qiblah and then sat down facing it and started to urinate. I said: \O Abu Abd al-Rahman! Is this not forbidden?\"" So he said: \""Yes! But it is forbidden to do this in the open air. When there is something obstructing you and the Qiblah"
"162","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us, \If we pour water on our private parts (during and after defecating)"
"163","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once it was mentioned to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that some people do not like facing the Qibla while defecating and their backs, so the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed them to defecate in a place where the faeces were facing the Qibla. Imam Darqutni states: In the chain of transmission of this tradition, there is a narrator named Khalid bin Abu Salat between the narrator named Khalid and the narrator named Arak."
"164","Narrated Khalid: Those people were present with Umar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: \Since I was young"
"165","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard about some people who disliked facing the Qiblah while defecating or urinating, so by the order of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) their places of defecation were turned towards the direction of the Qiblah. This tradition is more authentic. This tradition has also been narrated by some other narrators."
"166","Khalid bin Abu Salat narrates: I was sitting next to Umar bin Abdul Aziz during his caliphate, and Arak bin Malik was also sitting next to him. Umar ibn Abdul Aziz said: \I have never turned my back towards the Qiblah while urinating or defecating for so long.\"" So Arak said: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated this hadith to me. She says: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to know about the opinion of some people"
"167","Arak bin Malik narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, she says: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, commanded: \Turn my toilet towards the Qiblah.\"" A narrator named Yahya bin Ishaq has narrated this: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) brought Tashrif and people were talking about the dislike of facing the Qiblah when urinating or defecating."""
"168","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: On the order of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his toilet was turned towards the Qibla, when he found out that some people disliked it."
"169","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on some errand. Shaykh Abul Hasan (Imam Darqutni) says: The narrator named Isa bin Abu Isa Hanat is weak."
"170","Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub Ansari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Do not face the Qiblah while defecating or urinating"
"171","Isa bin Abu 'Isa narrates: I said to Imam Sha'bi: I am very surprised at the saying of Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) and the tradition narrated by Nafi' on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Umar (RA). Imam Shaabi inquired: What have these two gentlemen stated? So I replied: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu says: Do not turn your back or turn towards the Qiblah (at the time of need). While Nafi has quoted this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, he says: \I saw the Holy Prophet"
"172","Wasee bin Hibban narrates: I have heard Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrating this, he says: Once I climbed onto the roof of Sayyida Hafsa's (RA) house, at a time when I thought that no one would leave the house at that time. When I noticed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting on two bricks facing towards the Holy House and performing his ablutions."
"173","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) brought a pot of water. This tradition has also been narrated along with other sources."
"174","Talha bin Nafi narrates: Sayyidna Abu Ayyub Ansari, Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari and Sayyidna Anas bin Malik Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them) have narrated this verse regarding the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) (the verse is:) “In it are those who love it: they purify themselves well, and Allah loves those who purify themselves well.” is.” The Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \O group of Ansar! Allah has highly praised you for attaining purity. What is your method of attaining purity?\"" He said: \""O Messenger of Allah! We perform ablution for prayer"
"175","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution with the water left by animals. The narrator of this hadeeth is Ibrahim bin Abi Hiyya, who is weak. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"176","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: It was asked: \O Messenger of Allah! Shall we perform ablution with the water left by the donkeys?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Perform ablution (also) with water from the hooves of animals.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Ibn Abi Habiba"
"177","This tradition is narrated from Dawud bin Husain along with another chain of transmission."
"178","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The price of a dog is impure and he himself is even more impure than that.\"" The narrator of this tradition"
"179","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited the houses of some Ansaris, the houses that were before their houses (he did not visit them there), so these people were surprised by this, they said: \O Messenger of Allah! You have visited the house of so-and-so and did not visit our house?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The reason for this is: There is a dog in your house.\"" He said: \""There is a cat in their house.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The cat is among the beasts.\"" Narrator Isa bin Musayb is unique in narrating this tradition and these hadiths are reliable in narrating."""
"180","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \A cat is a beast.\"" In one tradition"
"181","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish"
"182","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish"
"183","On the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, this hadith was narrated about a dog: When a dog puts its mouth into a vessel, he says: \The contents of it should be washed away"
"184","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"185","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The method of purifying a person's vessel"
"186","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The way to purify a vessel"
"187","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"188","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"189","The same hadith is also narrated along with another authority, but it contains the words: \The first time to be cleansed with mud.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
"190","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"191","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mughfil (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the killing of dogs. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \What is the benefit of this to the people?\"" Then the Prophet (PBUH) allowed dogs to be kept to protect the hunting dogs and goats. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"192","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a person's dish"
"193","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about dogs: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"194","The same hadith is also narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \That person should wash it three times (the narrator is doubtful"
"195","This same tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission, in which the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \You should wash it seven times.\"" This tradition is more authentic."""
"196","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"197","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: \If a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"198","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes a cat would come to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would hold out a vessel to it and it would drink water from it, and then he would perform ablution with the water from the cat's paws. A narrator named Abu Bakr narrates: The narrator of this tradition is Yaqub, this is Qazi Abu Yusuf, and the narrator named Abd Rabbah is Abdullah bin Saeed Maqbri, who is weak."
"199","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu has this saying about the cat's dung: \This water should be drained away and this vessel should be washed once (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words:) twice.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\""."""
"200","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates this about Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, he said: \When a cat puts its mouth in a vessel"
"201","Muhammad bin Sireen narrates the saying of Sayyidna Abu Hurairah Radiyallahu Anhu: He said this about cats: \If it puts its mouth into a vessel"
"202","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) said this about a cat: \When it puts its mouth in a vessel"
"203","Hasan bin Ali narrates: I heard Ata narrate this: He said this about cats: \When it puts its mouth in a vessel"
"204","Saeed bin Musayb says: \A man should wash it twice (the narrator doubts perhaps these are the words:) three times.\"""""
"205","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a dog puts its mouth in a vessel"
"206","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says this about a cat: \When it puts its mouth in a vessel"
"207","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \The vessel will be washed when a cat puts it in its mouth"
"208","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a cat puts its mouth in it"
"209","This tradition is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition along with another chain of transmission."""
"210","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (RA) says: \The vessel in which the cat puts its mouth should be washed seven times.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\"" and not authentically transmitted."""
"211","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"212","The sons of Taos narrate this about their father: He used to wash the pot seven times, even after a cat's mouth, like a dog's mouth. Ibn Jaraj narrates: I asked Ata: What is the ruling of the cat? So he said: \It is like a dog.\"" Or perhaps he said: \""It's worse than that.\"""""
"213","Mujahid says about putting a cat's mouth in a vessel: \Wash this vessel seven times.\"""""
"214","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and I used to perform ablution from the same vessel, from which the cat had previously drunk water. This tradition is \correct\""."""
"215","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution using the same vessel, from which the cat had previously drunk water."
"216","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \This (cat) is not impure"
"217","It was narrated about Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA): Once a cat ate some of Harisa, Sayyida Ayesha (RA) later ate some of it and said: \I saw the Prophet (PBUH)"
"218","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pour the pot towards the cat and the cat would drink from it, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform ablution through the cat's hooves."
"219","Narrated Sayyidah Kabsha bint Ka'b, who was the wife of one of the sons of Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah: Once Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah entered the house of Ansari, and this woman kept ablution water for him. Meanwhile, a cat came to him to drink water from it, so Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) poured the pot towards him, and the cat drank the water. That woman narrates: When Sayyiduna Abu Qutada (RA) saw me looking at him with great attention, he inquired: \O my niece! Are you surprised at this?\"" The woman narrates: I answered: \""Yes!\"" So Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (RA) said: \""The Prophet (PBUH) said this: This (cat) is not impure"
"220","Imam Jafar Sadiq, may God have mercy on him, narrates this on the authority of his father (Imam Muhammad Baqir, may God have mercy on him): Sayyiduna Ali (may God be pleased with him) (or perhaps Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him) was asked about the cat's hoof, and he said: \It is among the beasts"
"221","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The companions of the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) searched for water for ablution, but they did not find it. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired: \Is there even a little water anywhere?\"" (He was present)"
"222","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \He who does not mention the name of Allah in the beginning"
"223","Rabi' bin Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather (on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \There is no ablution for a person who does not recite the name of Allah at the beginning of it (i.e. does not recite Bismillah).\"""""
"224","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would touch (the bowl of ablution) he used to recite Bismillah first. A narrator named Abu Badr has described this (that is, these words are in the hadith): \When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would get up for ablution"
"225","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates his father's statement regarding his grandmother: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \There is no prayer for a person who does not perform ablution"
"226","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"227","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this on the authority of his grandmother, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \There is no prayer without ablution"
"228","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding his grandmother: He heard his father Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr radi Allahu anhu narrating this, he says: I heard the Prophet sallallahu alaihi wasallam saying: \The person who does not perform ablution does not have his prayer"
"229","Rabah bin Abd al-Rahman narrates this regarding his grandmother: He heard his father Saeed bin Zayd bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, narrate this, he says: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this: \The person who does not perform ablution does not have his prayer"
"230","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"231","Sayyiduna Abdullah (Bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him) narrates: I heard the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: \When a person starts performing ablution"
"232","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever performs ablution and recites the name of Allah (i.e. Bismillah)"
"233","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever performs ablution and recites the name of Allah at the beginning of ablution"
"234","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \For one who cannot find water"
"235","This same hadith along with another chain of transmission is related to Musaib as a \suspended\"" hadith"
"236","Narrated Ikramah: \Nabeez is a means of ablution for a person who does not have anything to perform ablution other than Nabeez (i.e. he does not have water).\"""""
"237","Ikramah states: \Whoever finds nothing else besides Nabeez"
"238","Narrated Ikramah: \Through water"
"239","Ikramah states: \A person who does not have water can perform ablution through Nabeez.\"""""
"240","Isa bin Ubaid narrates: I heard Ikrima, he was asked about a person: Who does not get water. Ikramah said: \That person should perform ablution through Nabeez.\"""""
"241","Ikrimah narrates this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): \A person who does not have water can perform ablution through water.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Ibn Muharr"
"242","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person does not get water"
"243","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may God be pleased with him) narrates this statement from Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (may God be pleased with him): On the night of the meeting with the Jinn, he performed ablution on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a nabid, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution with it. A narrator named Ibn Lahiyyah is not considered authentic. There is also a saying: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA) was not present with the Prophet (PBUH) on the night of the meeting with the jinn. Alqamah bin Qais has narrated it in the same way. Abu Ubaidah bin Abdullah and other narrators have narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu, he says: \I was not present on the night of the meeting with the jinn.\"""""
"244","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates the statement of Sayyidna Abdullah Bin Mas’ud (RA): Once he went out with the Prophet (PBUH), it was the night when he met the jinn, and the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: “O Ibn Mas’ud! Do you have water?” Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \I have Nabeez in a vessel.\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Pour it over me.\"" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through it and said: \""It is also something to drink and purification can also be achieved from it.\"" A narrator named Ibn Lahiyyah is unique in narrating this tradition and it is a weak narrator."""
"245","Alqamah bin Qays narrates: I asked Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud, may Allah be pleased with him: \When the representatives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) attended the service of the Prophet"
"246","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abdul Aziz narrated from us, he said: Ali bin Al-Jaad narrated from us, he was informed by Shu’ba, he from Amr bin Murrah, he said: I said to Abu Ubaidah, may God be pleased with him: “Did Abdullah bin Mas’ud participate in the night of the jinn?” He said: \No.\"""""
"247","Narrated Amr bin Murrah: I asked Abu Ubaidah: \Was Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud RA the night he met the jinn?\"" So they answered: \""No!\"" It is narrated in another hadith: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: On the night of the meeting with the jinn"
"248","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission, but its narrators have been cross-examined."
"249","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) inquired on the night of his meeting with the jinn: \Do you have any water?\"" So they said: \""No!\"" I have a prophet. The narrator narrates: Then this prophet was brought and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through him."""
"250","Abu Wail narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud radi Allahu anhu narrating this, he says: I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of his meeting with the jinn. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) asked me at some part of the night: \O Ibn Mas'ud! Do you have water?\"" I said: \""No! By Allah! O Messenger of Allah! I have only Nabeez in the vessel.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""The date palm is pure and its water is purifying.\"" Then the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution through it. A narrator named Hussain bin Ubaidullah used to invent and narrate traditions on the authority of Taqqa narrators."""
"251","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me. He said: \Take a vessel of water with you.\"" Then you continued walking"
"252","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: On the night of my meeting with the jinn, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked me to bring water for ablution. This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Thaqafi on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu: It is unknown. According to one view his name is Amr and according to another view his name is Abdullah bin Amr."
"253","Abu Khaldah narrates: I asked Abul Aaliyah: A person who does not have water with him, but he has Nabeez, can he perform Ghusl Janabat through this Nabeez? So Abul Alia replied: \No!\"" So I mentioned to him the hadith about the meeting with the jinn"
"254","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): He did not think there was anything wrong with performing ablution through the Prophet."
"255","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): He said: \There is no harm in performing ablution through water.\"""""
"256","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is no prayer for a person who does not perform ablution"
"257","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"258","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called for water for ablution, he performed ablution with it once, and then he said: \This is the method of ablution without which Allah does not accept the prayer.\"" Then he called for water and performed ablution twice with it"
"259","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"260","The same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA), but some of its narrators have been declared weak."
"261","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution once and said: \This is the ablution without which Allah does not accept the prayer.\"" Then he performed ablution twice"
"262","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): “Whoever performs ablution once, this is the method of ablution that is necessary, and whoever performs ablution twice, he will receive double the reward, and whoever performs ablution three times, then this is my method and that of the prophets who came before me.”"
"263","Sayyiduna Abi bin Ka'b (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) called for water and performed ablution with it once, and then said: \This is the method of ablution. Whoever does not perform ablution in this way"
"264","Ubaidullah bin Abu Rafi' narrated this statement of his father: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform ablution three times, and I saw him perform ablution once."
"265","Thabit Samali narrates: I asked Imam Abu Ja'far (Imam Muhammad Baqir) this: Has Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrated this hadith to you? The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution once, once and twice, twice and three times, then Imam Abu Ja'far (i.e. Imam Baqir) replied: \Yes!\"" The narrator of this tradition"
"266","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Jahni, who was shown the way to call the call to prayer in a dream, narrates: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, he washed his blessed face three times, washed both arms twice, and washed both feet twice. Ibn Ayaina narrated it in the same way, by the way, its narrator is Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd al-Mazni, may God be pleased with him, and these are not the Companions who were taught how to give the call to prayer in a dream."
"267","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zayd Jahni, may God be pleased with him, who was shown the way to call the Adhan in a dream, narrates: I saw the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when he performed ablution, he washed his blessed face three times, washed both arms twice, and both feet twice, and wiped his head twice."
"268","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiped his head and washed both his feet twice.\"""""
"269","The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, however, it contains these words: \The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his face three times and washed both his arms twice.\"""""
"270","Amr bin Yahya narrates the statement of his father: Amr bin Abu Hasan Mazni came to the service of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu. Amr ibn Abu Hasan requested: \Can you show us this? How did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution?\"" So Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu replied: \""Yes!\"" Then Sayyiduna Abdullah called for a vessel of water"
"271","Hamran narrates: One day Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani asked for water for ablution, then he performed ablution, washed both hands three times, then rinsed, then poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed his right arm up to the elbow three times and then washed his left arm in the same way, then he wiped his head, then he washed his right foot up to the ankle three times and then his left foot in the same way. Washed, and narrated this: \I saw the Holy Prophet"
"272","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, he used to pour water up to his elbows. The narrator of this tradition, Ibn Aqeel, is not authentic."
"273","A narrator named Ubaidullah has narrated this on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Rafi': When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he would move his ring (while washing his hands). Both the narrator of this tradition, Muammar and his father, are weak and this tradition is not authentic."
"274","Hamran narrates: He heard Sayyidna Uthman Ghani Radiyallahu Anhu, Sayyidna Uthman Ghani Radiyallahu Anhu said: \You people come forward"
"275","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Grinding and pouring water into the nose is an obligatory part of ablution.\"""""
"276","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, but it contains these words: \This is a part of ablution"
"277","As for the hadeeth narrated by Ibn Jarij on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, which is about ablution and putting water in the nose, then it is: Ibn Jarij narrates: Sulaiman bin Musa narrated this, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever performs ablution"
"278","Sulaiman bin Musa narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever performs ablution"
"279","Sulaiman bin Musa narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever performs ablution"
"280","Sulaiman ibn Musa al-Shami narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this, followed by the previous hadith."
"281","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \Whoever performs ablution"
"282","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: It is Sunnah to rinse (during ablution) and pour water into the nose. The narrator of this tradition is Ismail bin Muslim \weak\""."""
"283","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA): One day he called for water for ablution and then called some of the companions of the Prophet (RA), then he poured water on his left hand through his right hand and washed it three times. He rinsed three times, then poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, three times, then he wiped his head, then he washed both his feet and cleaned them well, then he narrated: \I saw the Prophet"
"284","Basar bin Saeed narrates: Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, came to the \Maqeed\"""
"285","Abu Anas narrates: Once Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) performed ablution in the sitting room, while some companions (RA) were present with him. Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (RA) washed each organ three times and then inquired: \Didn't you see the Prophet (PBUH) performing ablution in the same way?\"" So these gentlemen answered: \""Yes!\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
"286","Abu Wail narrates: I saw Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, he performed ablution and washed both hands three times, then washed his face three times, then rinsed his nose three times, poured water into his nose three times, then washed both arms three times, then wiped his head and the outside and inside of both ears, and then washed both feet three times, then he crossed his fingers, and when he had washed his face, he then washed his face three times. He had also shaved his beard, then Sayyidna Uthman Ghani (RA) narrated this: \I saw the Prophet (PBUH)"
"287","Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates: I saw Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution, first he washed both hands three times, then he rinsed, he poured water into his nose, he did this three times, then he washed his face three times, he washed both arms three times, then he wiped his head and then he wiped the inside and outside of both ears, he shaved his beard three times and then he washed both feet, he also washed his toes three times. and said: \I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform (ablution) in the same way as I have performed this (ablution).\"" The words of these two traditions are very close."""
"288","Sayyidah Rabi bint Mu'awz (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and after washing his arms, he wiped his head with a cotton swab."
"289","Sayyidah Rabi bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to visit us, and when he performed ablution, he would wipe his head with the remaining water after washing both arms and wipe in this way. After that, a narrator named Abdullah bin Dawud showed him by wiping and bringing his two hands from the back of the head to the front and then moving both hands from the front to the back of the head."
"290","A narrator named Ziyad narrates: A man came to the service of Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) and asked him about performing ablution and said: \Should I start with the right hand or should I start with the left hand?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali reprimanded him and then he called for water and (doing ablution) washed his left hand before his right hand."""
"291","Narrated Ziyad: A man asked Sayyiduna Ali: \Can I wash my left hand before my right hand during ablution?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali rebuked him"
"292","A narrator named Ziyad narrates: Sayyiduna Ali was asked: \Sayyidna Abu Huraira always washes the right organ first in ablution?\"" So Sayyiduna Ali called for water and started from the left side while doing ablution."""
"293","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \When I perform ablution"
"294","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"295","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says: \I do not care about this"
"296","Sayyiduna Abdullah (bin Abbas may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this: \There is nothing wrong with that. You wash (in ablution) both your feet before your arms.\"" This tradition is \""transmitted\"" and it is not proven."""
"297","It was narrated about Sayyidna Abdullah bin Masoud (RA): He was asked about a person who washes his left side first while performing ablution, then Sayyidna Abdullah (RA) said: \There is nothing wrong with that.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
"298","A narrator named Abd Khair narrated this about Sayyiduna Ali: “He first washed his two hands while doing ablution, then rinsed them three times and poured water into his nose, then washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, then wiped his head three times and then washed both feet three times, and then said: ‘Whoever likes to see the way of ablution of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, let him. Look at this way.'\ Shuaib"
"299","Abd Khair narrates: One day Sayyiduna Ali (RA) sat outside in the field after performing the Fajr prayer, then he said to his servant: \Bring water for ablution!\"" The servant brought water in a pot and brought a saucer with him. We were looking at Sayyiduna Ali"
"300","Abd Khair narrates: Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said this: \The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed all his limbs three times while performing ablution and took fresh water for his head.\"""""
"301","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him: When he performed ablution, he washed his hands three times, poured water into his nose three times, rinsed his mouth three times, then washed his face three times, washed each of his two arms three times, wiped his head three times, then washed his feet three times, then said: \I saw the Prophet"
"302","Shaqiq bin Salamah narrates: I saw Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may God be pleased with him, he performed ablution, then he rinsed first, then he poured water into his nose, he did this three times, then he washed his face three times, then he trimmed his beard three times, then he washed both arms three times, then he wiped his head three times, he washed both feet three times, and then he narrated this matter to the Prophet, peace be upon him. I have seen him doing (ablution) like that.”"
"303","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani: He called for water for ablution, then washed both his hands three times, then washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, then wiped his head three times, then washed both feet three times and said: \I saw the Prophet"
"304","Narrated by Ibn Daraa: I entered the house of Sayyidna Uthman Ghani, may Allah be pleased with him, and he heard my voice saying that I was performing ablution, so he called out: \O Muhammad!\"" I said: \""I am here!\"" He said: \""Shall I not tell you the method of ablution of the Holy Prophet?\"" I replied: \""Yes!\"" So Sayyidna Uthman Ghani said: \""I remember well about the Holy Prophet"
"305","It is narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani: He performed ablution in a maqa'id (open space), in Madinah the maqa'id (open space) is where the funeral prayer is performed near the mosque. Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani first washed his hands three times, then poured water into his nose three times, then rinsed his mouth three times, washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head three times, then washed both feet three times. A person greeted him, he was still performing ablution, Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani did not respond to the greeting until he finished performing ablution, when he finished, he presented an excuse to him while talking to him and said: \I did not respond to the greeting because I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: 'Whoever performs ablution in this way and does not utter a word during ablution and this (After ablution) read: \""I bear witness that there is no god but Allah"
"306","Abd Khair narrated this about Sayyiduna Ali: \While performing ablution"
"307","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: “Whoever performs ablution and washes his hands three times, pours water into his nose three times, rinses his mouth three times, washes his face and both arms three times, wipes his head three times, washes his feet three times, then recites: ‘I testify that there is no god but Allah, and Sayyidna Muhammad. (The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) is His special servant and messenger.''"
"308","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him): Once he came with some of his companions and sat in a muqa'id (open space), he asked for water for ablution, then he washed both his hands three times, rinsed his mouth three times, poured water into his nose three times, washed his face three times, washed both arms three times, wiped his head once, then washed his two feet three times, and then said this Ki: \I have seen the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution in the same way. I was already in a state of ablution"
"309","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to wash each organ twice while performing ablution."
"310","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu has narrated this: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) used to perform ablution twice."
"311","Sayyiduna Abu Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution for prayer, he would move the ring on his finger."
"312","Ghulam Safina, the slave of Sayyidah Umm Salama (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with one \Mud\"" of water and performed Ghusl with one \""Sa'\"" of water."""
"313","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution with about one mudd of water and performed ghusl with about one saa of water."
"314","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to perform ablution with two \liters\"" of water and one \""Sa'\"" with eight liters of water. A narrator named Musa bin Nasr is unique in narrating this tradition and this Sahib is weak."""
"315","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Ten things are part of nature: trimming the moustache"
"316","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Harith bin Jaz Zubaydi (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \For (some) heels and soles are the destruction of Hell.\"""""
"317","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he used to rub his toes (toes) and touch his heels, and he used to say: \What do you rub between your toes"
"318","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Make a cross between your fingers, Allah will not cross between them on the Day of Resurrection with fire.”"
"319","This is narrated on the authority of Sayyidna Rifa'a bin Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him): Sayyidna Rifa'a (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyidna Malik bin Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) are brothers and participated in the Battle of Badr. Sayyidna Rafi' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once we were sitting with the Holy Prophet (may Allah's prayers and peace be upon him). He prayed facing the Qiblah, when he finished the prayer, he came and greeted the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and also greeted the people present. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: \You must go back and pray"
"320","Imam Zain al-Abidin (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated this on the authority of Sayyida Rabi bint Mu’awz: He asked Sayyida Rabi’ (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) about the manner of ablution of the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him), and Sayyida Rabi’ (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him) replied: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit her, she used to keep ablution water for the Prophet (may God’s prayers and peace be upon him). Imam Zain al-Abidin, may God have mercy on him, narrates: Once I came to this woman, and she took out a vessel in front of me and told me: “In this vessel, I used to draw water for the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, to perform ablution. He washed both arms, then wiped his head from front to back and from back to front, then he washed both feet, then this woman said: \Your cousin also came to me"
"321","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator narrated it as follows: However"
"322","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator has quoted this tradition as \""Marfu'\"" tradition and it is his illusion. This is the correct thing"
"323","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator has quoted this tradition as a \""marfu' hadith in the same way"
"324","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\""."""
"325","Ja'far ibn Muhammad al-Wasti narrated that Musa ibn Ishaq narrated to him, he said that Abu Bakr told him that Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated from Ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to wipe both ears and say, \These are the two parts of the head.\"" This hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar as a \""suspended\"" hadith."""
"326","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) used to wipe both ears and say: \These two are part of the head.\"""""
"327","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"328","Hilal bin Usamah narrates: I heard Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may God be pleased with him) say: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"329","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"330","It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He said: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Muhammad bin Fazl Muhammad bin Fazl bin Atiya"
"331","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"332","The same tradition is also narrated along with some other traditions, in which the narrator is delusional at some point. The subject of this tradition also exists, but the narrator narrating it is obsolete. However, more accurately, this tradition is transmitted as a \messenger\"" tradition from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with reference to a narrator named Sulaiman bin Musa."""
"333","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"334","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \(When performing ablution) rinse and pour water into the nose and the two ears are part of the head (ie the ears will be wiped like the head).\"" The narrator of this hadith is Rabi bin Badr."""
"335","Sulaiman bin Musa narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"336","Sulaiman bin Musa quoted the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"337","The same tradition is also narrated with reference to Sulaiman bin Musa along with another chain of transmission: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"338","The same hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Solomon bin Musa along with another chain of transmission: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"339","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Both ears are part of the head.\"" Narrator named Ali bin Asim has been deceived in quoting this tradition"
"340","Sayyida Aisha Sadiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever performs ablution"
"341","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person performs ablution"
"342","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, has narrated the same thing with reference to the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but in it there are these words:"
"343","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Grinding and putting water in the nose is a part of ablution without which ablution is not complete"
"344","A narrator named Ata has narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Grinding and pouring water into the nose is one of the acts of ablution"
"345","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: \In ablution"
"346","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \It is Sunnah to rinse and pour water into the nose"
"347","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person performs ablution"
"348","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"349","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"350","The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission and one of its narrators is Muhammad bin Ziyad Matrook Hadith. This same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated as a \suspended\"" hadith on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"351","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The same tradition has also been narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA)."""
"352","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rinse (while performing ablution) and pour water into the nose, both ears are part of the head. One of the narrators of this hadith, Amr Ibn Husayn, and the other narrator, Ibn Alashah, are weak."
"353","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" One of the narrators of this tradition"
"354","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Bakhtari bin Ubayd Zaeef and his father is unknown."""
"355","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This hadith has been narrated by a narrator named Ali Ibn Jafar as a \""marfu'\"" hadith"
"356","Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) says: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This tradition is \""suspended\"". Some other narrators have followed suit. The same hadith is also narrated from Sayyidna Abu Umamah Bahli (may Allah be pleased with him)."""
"357","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" (He has also stated this:) The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe the corners of both eyes and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe his blessed head once. The narrator of this tradition"
"358","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu has quoted the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"359","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA) has quoted this saying of the Prophet (PBUH). The narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words: Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" That is"
"360","It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrators have narrated it in the same way with reference to the narrator named Hamad"
"361","A narrator named Shahr bin Hushab has narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA): Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (RA) narrated the method of ablution of the Holy Prophet (SAW) and said: When the Prophet (SAW) used to perform ablution, he used to wipe the corners of his eyes with water. Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu also stated: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" Sulaiman bin Harb has stated: \""Both ears are part of the head.\"" This is the saying of Sayyidina Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu"
"362","Daalaj ibn Ahmad narrates: I asked Musa ibn Haroon about this hadith, and he said: \There is no truth in it"
"363","Sayyidna Rashid bin Saad narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" This hadith is \""transmitted\"""
"364","Rashid bin Saad narrates on the authority of Sayyiduna Abu Umamah, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"""""
"365","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah Radiyallahu Anhu narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" The narrator of this tradition"
"366","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Both ears are part of the head.\"" A narrator of this tradition"
"367","``Urwa bin Qubaysa, on the authority of an Ansari, quoted the saying of Sayyiduna Uthman Ghani (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding his father: \You people know this! The two ears are part of the head.\"""""
"368","Narrated Umrah: I asked Sayyida Aisha about the two ears, and she replied: \These two ears are part of the head.\"" Then he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe the outer and inner parts of both ears while performing ablution. One of the narrators of this tradition is Yaman \""weak\""."""
"369","Abd Khair narrates: Once Sayyiduna Ali (RA) came and sat in the courtyard after offering the Fajr prayer, then he said to his servant: \Bring me water for ablution!\"" The servant brought water to you in a vessel"
"370","Ayyub bin Abdullah narrates: I saw Hasan bin Abul Hasan, he asked for water for ablution, and a large pot of water was brought to him, then the water was poured into the bowl, he first washed both hands three times, then rinsed them three times, then poured water into his nose three times, then washed his face three times, then washed both arms up to the elbows three times, then wiped his head, then wiped both ears. And trimmed his beard, then washed both his feet up to the ankles, then narrated this: Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik Radiyallahu Anhu narrated this hadith to me."
"371","Sayyidah Rabi' bint Mu'awz (RA) narrates: I saw the Prophet (PBUH) performing ablution. He (PBUH) wiped the front and back of his head and both ears, then he (PBUH) inserted his index fingers and wiped the outside and inside of the ear with them."
"372","Hameed narrates: Sayyiduna Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, used to wipe the top and inside of his ears when performing ablution, and then he would say: \I saw the Prophet"
"373","Hameed narrates: I saw Sayyidna Anas bin Malik performing ablution, he wiped the inside and outside of both his ears and then said: \Sayyidna Abdullah bin Mas'ud used to order (to wipe both ears).\"""""
"374","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, he would gently touch both his cheeks and then use his fingers to stroke his beard from below."
"375","Narrated by Nafi: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) used to perform ablution (after that he narrated it according to the previous hadith). However, he did not quote this hadith as a \marfu'\"" hadith and that is correct."""
"376","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that: When he used to wipe his head, he would lift his cap and wipe the front part of his head."
"377","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed me: \When we perform ablution for prayer"
"378","Abu Ammar narrates: He has had the privilege of visiting some of the companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. (He then narrated the entire incident). Sayyiduna Amr bin Absa (RA) narrated: \I said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me something about ablution!\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Whoever performs ablution"
"379","This tradition is narrated along with another document. Its certificate is \proven\"" and \""authentic\""."""
"380","Abd al-Rahman bin Sabat narrated this on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA), or perhaps on the authority of the brother of Sayyidna Abu Umamah (RA): Once the Prophet (PBUH) saw some people (doing ablution), the water of one of them had not reached the heel of a dirham, or perhaps the size of a nail, so the Prophet (PBUH) began to say: It's a waste.\ (The narrator narrates:) \""A man should examine this"
"381","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: Once a person came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he had performed ablution and left a part of his foot as much as a nail (the water did not reach there), so the Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \Go back and perform ablution well.\"" A narrator named Jarir bin Hazim is unique in narrating this tradition from Qatadah and this narrator is reliable."""
"382","Salim, on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, has quoted the statement of Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, on the authority of Sayyiduna Omar, who said: \Once I was sitting with the Prophet"
"383","The meaning of this hadith is close to each other, one of its narrators, Waza' bin Nafi', has been described as weak in the knowledge of hadith."
"384","Ubaid bin Umayr narrates: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab once saw a person whose feet were partially dry and while performing ablution, water did not reach there. Then Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered him: \Let him wash this dry place and pray again.\"""""
"385","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab (RA): Once he saw a person whose back part of his feet was dry, the water did not reach there, then Sayyidna Umar (RA) said to him: \Have you joined the prayer with this ablution?\"" He said: \""O Commander of the Faithful! It is very cold and I have nothing to stop it.\"" Sayyiduna Umar"
"386","Alaa bin Ziyad narrates the following on the authority of one of the Companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: Once, the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the Companions of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. You had bathed, but part of your body was left dry where the water did not reach. We said: \O Messenger of Allah! This part has remained dry"
"387","Alaa bin Ziyad narrated: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat, then he saw a little dry spot on his neck. This tradition is transmitted and it is correct."
"388","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a special cloth with which he used to dry his limbs during ablution. The narrator of this tradition is Abu Mu'adh, Sulaiman bin Arqam and it is obsolete."
"389","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution, I took the water left over from his ablution and poured it into my well."
"390","Sayyiduna Osama bin Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates about the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of his father, Sayyidna Zayd bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him): When the first revelation was revealed to him, Sayyidna Jibreel (peace be upon him) attended the service of the Prophet (peace be upon him) and showed him how to perform ablution and pray. When he finished his ablution, he took water in a chloe and sprinkled it on his private parts."
"391","Sayyiduna Osama Bin Zayd Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: When Sayyidna Jibraeel (peace be upon him) was revealed to the Prophet (peace be upon him) (in the early days), he showed the Prophet (peace be upon him) how to perform ablution."
"392","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa Radiyallahu Anha narrates: \Ghusl becomes wajib when the private part meets the private part.\"" When I and the Prophet (PBUH) used to do this"
"393","It was narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA): She was asked about a person who has intercourse with his wife and does not ejaculate, then Sayida Aisha (RA) said: \When I and the Prophet (PBUH) used to do this"
"394","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (may God be pleased with him) narrates: Umm Kulthum (may God be pleased with him) narrated to me on the authority of Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with him), a person asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) about a man who has intercourse with his wife and then (ends intercourse) before ejaculation, \Would it be necessary to perform ghusl on him?\"" So at that time"
"395","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) offered the morning prayer. You had performed Ghusl Janabat, a verma-sized part of your blessed body was left dry where the water did not reach. It was reported: \O Messenger of Allah! The water did not reach this place.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dripped the water from his hair on that spot and turned his hand there"
"396","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat, then he saw a small area on his skin where the water had not reached, so he squeezed some water from his hair and applied that water to that place."
"397","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person has intercourse with a woman"
"398","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \When a man has intercourse with a woman"
"399","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Ghusl becomes necessary for four reasons: because of Janabat"
"400","Sayyidna Jabir bin Abdullah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Janabat does not affect water"
"401","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) states: \There is no janabat in four things: in man"
"402","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform Ghusl Janabat, first of all he would wash both his hands, then he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, then he would insert his hand into the blessed vessel and then run the water through the roots of his hair, until when he felt that he had washed his skin thoroughly, he would fill both hands with water three times. He used to pour it on his head, then wash the whole body afterwards."
"403","Jami bin Umayr narrates: Once I attended Sayyida Aisha's service with my mother and aunt, and Sayyida Aisha said: \The Prophet"
"404","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Sayyida Maimunah (RA) told me this, once when the Prophet (PBUH) began to perform Ghusl Janabat, I came close to him, then he washed both his hands two or maybe three times. What, then performed ablution like the ablution of prayer, then you washed your whole body with water in both palms, then you moved away from that place a little and you washed both your feet, then I brought a handkerchief to you (so that you could wipe your body) so you did not accept it."
"405","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this statement of his aunt Sayyida Maimunah (RA), she says: \I kept water for the bath of the Holy Prophet (PBUH)"
"406","Sayyida Umm Salma (RA) narrates: \My hair used to be tightly tied in the form of braids. I asked the Prophet (PBUH) about this"
"407","Muhammad bin Sirin narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) declared it Sunnah to pour water into the nose three times in the Ghusl of Janabat."
"408","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"409","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) made it obligatory for a Janabi person to perform ablution three times and pour water into the nose. Imam Darqutni states: This hadith is invalid. No one narrated it except a narrator named Barqa, and this narrator named Barqa used to make hadiths on his own. The correct tradition is the one narrated by a narrator named Waqiyyah, which we have previously quoted as a “Mursal” tradition on the authority of Ibn Sirin: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made it Sunnah to pour water into the nose three times in the state of Ghusl Janabat."
"410","Ibn Sirin narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed to pour water into the nose three times in the state of Ghusl Janabat."
"411","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Abbas (RA) narrates: \If a person washes his face during Ghusl Janabat (and forgets to put water in his nose)"
"412","Aisha bint Ajard narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma: \A person will perform the prayer again in the case of forgetting to perform ablution in Janabat and putting water in the nose"
"413","Aisha bint Ajard has narrated this statement of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas Radiyallahu Anhuma: \A person will repeat the prayer only when he is on his side.\"""""
"414","Aisha bint Ajard narrated this about a Janbi person: \Whoever (while taking bath) forgets to rinse and put water in his nose.\"" That woman narrates: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) said: \""He will rinse"
"415","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) instructed us to rinse and pour water into the nose. This tradition is also transmitted along with another chain of transmission and it is transmitted as a \suspended\"" tradition. However"
"416","The same hadith along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Huraira, but there is some difference in its chain of transmission. Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (R.A.) is not mentioned in one chain of transmission."
"417","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Sarjis (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade this: \A man should bathe with the water left over from a woman's bath"
"418","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Sarjis Radiyallahu Anhu narrates: \A woman can perform ablution or ghusl with the water left over from a man's bath or ablution"
"419","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Menstruating women and menstruating women should not read the Qur'an at all.\"""""
"420","The same hadith has been narrated along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"421","The same hadith regarding Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) has been narrated along with another chain of transmission and it has also been followed."
"422","This tradition is narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA)."
"423","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \A foreigner should not read the Qur'an at all.\"" This tradition is narrated along with another document."""
"424","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates the saying of the Prophet (PBUH): \A pregnant person and a menstruating woman should not read the Qur'an at all.\"""""
"425","Abu Zarif Hamdani narrates: Once we were with Sayyiduna Ali (RA) in an open field, Sayyidna Ali (RA) went to the edge of this field. By Allah! I don't know, did they urinate or defecate, they called for a vessel of water, then they washed both their hands and then joined them both and recited the first part of the Qur'an and then said: \You can recite the Qur'an until a person is afflicted with Janabat"
"426","According to a hadith, it was narrated from Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him). According to the second chain of transmission, this is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari, may Allah be pleased with him, who narrates: The Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, said: \O Ali! I am pleased with you with what I am pleased with myself"
"427","Sayyiduna Abdullah Ghafqi narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate something and then he said: \Tonic the veil for me so that I may take a bath!\"" I inquired of you: \""Are you in a state of janabat?\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Yes!\"" Later"
"428","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Malik Ghafqi narrates: He heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, say this from Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him: \When I perform ablution in the state of Janabat"
"429","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: There was nothing that prevented the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from reciting the Qur’an, except when he was in a state of janabat. A narrator named Sufyan narrates: Shu'ba said to me: \I have not narrated a better hadith than him.\"""""
"430","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"" The evidence of this tradition is excellent. Some other narrators did not mention Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas in his chain of transmission."""
"431","It is narrated on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahha, may Allah be pleased with him: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, has prohibited us from saying: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"""""
"432","Ikramah narrates: Once Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha was sleeping by the side of his wife, he got up and went to his maidservant who was at the edge of the house and started having intercourse with her. His wife was frightened in a dream. When she went out, Sayyidna Abdullah bin Rawaha (RA) had finished with the company and was coming back. He was confronted by his wife who was holding a knife, so Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahha (RA) said: \What happened?\"" So his wife replied: \""What is the matter"
"433","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas: Once Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah entered the house (after that he narrated the entire incident, in which these words are:) Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Rawahah narrated that: The Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade: \A person should recite the Qur'an in a state of janabat.\"""""
"434","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu states: \A menstruating woman"
"435","Abdullah bin Abu Bakr narrates this statement of his father: The letter that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote to Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm, may Allah be pleased with him, also contained the following: \Touch the Qur'an only when you are ablution.\"" This hadith is \""Mussal\"" and its narrator is \""Thiqa\""."""
"436","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad narrates: The letter that the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to Sayyiduna Amr bin Hazm (RA), when he sent him to Najran, contained the following:"
"437","Salim narrates on the authority of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar) that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""
"438","Abdullah ibn Abu Bakr and Muhammad ibn Abu Bakr narrate this on the authority of their father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wrote a letter to him, which also said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""
"439","Abu Bakr bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, narrates the statement of his grandfather: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, wrote this letter to the people of Yemen, which also said: \Only a person who is ablution should touch the Qur'an.\"""""
"440","Sayyiduna Hakeem bin Hizam (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said to him: \Touch the Qur'an only when you are in the state of ablution.\"""""
"441","Narrated Anas bin Malik: Sayyidna Umar came out with a sword hanging around his neck and was told: \Your brother-in-law and your sister have become ungodly (i.e. they have accepted Islam).\"" So Sayyiduna Umar (R.A.) came to them both"
"442","Alqamah narrates: Once we were on a journey with Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him. So Sayyiduna Salman Farsi Radiyallahu Anhu said: \You ask me"
"443","Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid narrates: Once we were with Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, he visited, he defecated, and when he came, I said: \O Abu Abdullah! It would be appropriate if you perform ablution"
"444","Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid narrates: Once we were traveling with Sayyiduna Salman Farsi, may Allah be pleased with him, he visited, he defecated, then when he came, I said: \O Abu Abdullah! Perform ablution so that we may inquire from you about some verses of the Qur'an.\"" So he said: \""You ask me"
"445","This tradition along with some other isnads is narrated on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid about Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"446","Regarding Alqamah and Aswad, it has been narrated about Sayyiduna Salman (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He recited a verse of the Qur'an while he was performing ablution. All these credentials are authentic."
"447","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) was asked about semen on clothes, and he said: \It is like mucus and saliva. That will be enough for you. Clean it with a piece of cloth or grass.\"" Only the narrator Ishaq has narrated this tradition as a \""marfu'\"" tradition."""
"448","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) about semen on clothes: He said: \It is like phlegm and saliva"
"449","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: I used to scrape semen from the clothes of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when it was dry, and if it was wet, I would wash it off."
"450","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: If I saw a stain (of semen) on the clothes of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I used to wash them. This tradition is authentic."
"451","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When semen got on the Prophet's clothes, he would wash them and go to pray, while she used to see the traces of washing on his clothes."
"452","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to think: \Clothes do not have Janabat"
"453","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had Janabat and he intended to sleep, he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, but if he intended to eat something in that state, he would wash both his palms and eat. This tradition is authentic."
"454","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep in the state of janabat, he would perform ablution like the ablution of prayer, and if he intended to eat something (in the state of janabat), he would wash both hands and eat that thing. This tradition is authentic."
"455","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to sleep in the state of Janabat, he would perform ablution before going to sleep, like the ablution of prayer, and if he intended to eat something while he was in the state of Janabat, he would wash both his hands and rinse them and eat that thing. This tradition is authentic."
"456","Sayyidna Sahl bin Sa'd (RA) narrates: Sayyidna Abi Bin Ka'b (RA) narrated to me: \Some people say: Ghusl is required due to ejaculation (although in reality) it was a leave given by the Prophet (PBUH) in the early days of Islam"
"457","Al-Zuhri narrates: I asked Urwa about a man who has intercourse, but does not ejaculate, and Urwa replied: \The opinion of the people is this"
"458","Sayyidna Ammar bin Yasir (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) came to me. I was drawing water from a bucket by the side of a well at that time. He said: \O Ammar! What are you doing?\"" I said: \""O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed to you! I want to wash off the phlegm on my clothes.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""O Ammar! Clothes are washed for five reasons: feces"
"459","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Beware of urine"
"460","Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \There is no harm in the urine of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"" The narrator of this tradition is weak."""
"461","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \There is nothing wrong with the urine of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"" This tradition is not authentically proven. Some of its narrators are weak and one narrator is obsolete. According to a saying"
"462","Sayyiduna Bara' (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There is nothing wrong with the fat of an animal whose meat is eaten.\"""""
"463","Abdullah bin Abu Qadah narrates this statement of his father: \There is no harm in the sight of the animal whose flesh is eaten.\"""""
"464","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Beware of urine"
"465","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Often the punishment of the grave is due to urine.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
"466","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this as a \Marfu'\"" tradition: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \""The punishment of the grave is due to urine"
"467","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) urinated on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I picked him up hard. In one hadith are the words: He said: \Leave it alone! For it does not eat"
"468","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this about the urine of a milk-drinking child: \Water should be poured over the child's urine"
"469","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Water will be sprinkled on the urine of a boy and the urine of a girl will be washed.\"""""
"470","Narrated Qatadah: \It is when they are not eating"
"471","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: When the urine of a minor child got on the blessed body of the Prophet (PBUH) or on his skin, he sprinkled water on the place where the urine had got on."
"472","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says this about the child's urine: \Water should be sprinkled on the part on which it is applied.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) has narrated this: The Holy Prophet (PBUH) did the same thing when Imam Hussain bin Ali (RA) got urine. The narrator of this tradition is Ibrahim"
"473","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: We used to come to the mosque of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and go to sleep. This tradition is authentic."
"474","Sayyiduna Anas (RA) narrates: I saw the Companions of the Holy Prophet (SAW) who used to get up to pray, and sometimes I even heard one of them snoring, but they would get up and pray again and not perform ablution again. A narrator named Ibn Mubarak has stated this: \For us"
"475","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Companions of the Holy Prophet (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) used to wait for the call to prayer until Isha, until their heads were bowed down (i.e. they fell asleep), then they would get up and perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. This tradition is authentically transmitted."
"476","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Some people from the ``Arina tribe came to Madinah to serve the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The climate there did not suit them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: \If you people want"
"477","Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once a villager came, he urinated in the mosque, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered that the place be dug up, and then a bucket of water be poured over it. The villager said: \O Messenger of Allah! A person loves some people"
"478","Sayyiduna Abdullah narrates: Once a villager attended the Prophet's service, he was an old man, he said: \O Sayyidna Muhammad! When will the Hour come?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""What have you prepared for this?\"" He replied: \""By Him Who sent you with the truth"
"479","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Muaqal (RA) narrates: Once a villager stood on the edge of the mosque, he removed his apron and urinated there, then the Prophet (PBUH) said: \Take out the dirt from the place where he urinated and throw water on that place.\"" The narrator of this hadith is Abdullah bin Muaqal al-Tabi and this hadith is \""Mursal\""."""
"480","Sayyidna Safwan bin Asal narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this: \There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave permission for a traveler to wipe his socks for three days. However"
"481","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who sees tari but does not remember Ihtlam. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a person who remembers this. Sayyidah Umm Salim Radiyallahu Anha said: \If a woman sees this thing? Will this ruling be required for her as well?\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Yes! Women are the aspect of men.\"""""
"482","Sayyidna Abdullah bin Zubair (RA) narrates: I heard Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) saying: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Ghusl is required in five cases: after Janabat"
"483","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (RA) narrates: Once he was sitting with the Prophet (PBUH), while a man came to the service of the Prophet (PBUH), he said: \O Messenger of Allah! What do you say about such a person? Who approaches a woman who is not lawful for him and what men do to women"
"484","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: \A prayer will not be repeated because of kissing.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. In the proof of this tradition"
"485","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet of Allah used to kiss me, then he (may Allah bless him and grant him peace) would go to pray and not perform ablution again."
"486","This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions, in one of which there are these words: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss while fasting. Imam Malik has quoted this saying of Imam Zuhri: \After kissing"
"487","Imam Malik narrates this statement of Ibn Shihab Zuhri, who says: \If a husband kisses his wife"
"488","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Messenger of Allah used to kiss one of his wives, then he (may God bless him and grant him peace) would perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. (After narrating this) Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) smiled. There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while he was fasting."
"489","It has been narrated about Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa: She came to know a saying of Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, that ablution is necessary after kissing, so Sayida Aisha said: \The Prophet"
"490","There are these words in a hadith: Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"""""
"491","Urwa bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A gentleman has narrated this: Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) was asked about a person who kisses his wife after performing ablution, so Sayyida Ayesha (may God be pleased with her) said: \The Prophet"
"492","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss me and then pray and not perform ablution again. The narrator of this hadeeth is Ghalib ibn Ubaidullah, and it is obsolete."
"493","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and then pray and not perform ablution again."
"494","Ata states: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is correct."""
"495","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then go to pray and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Urwa narrates: I said to Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa, may God be pleased with her: \Who else could that woman be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled. There are these words in a hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then pray and not perform ablution again. (The narrator says:) So I said: \""Who else could that woman be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled."""
"496","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast and perform ablution before praying, then if any of his wives came in front of him, he would kiss her and then perform the prayer (i.e. he would not perform ablution again). Narrated Urwa: I said to him: \Who else can she be besides you?\"" So Sayyida Aisha smiled."""
"497","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution, then kiss his wife, and then pray and would not perform ablution again. Both of them have the same word."
"498","This tradition is also narrated along with another document. Sufyan Al-Thawri, who has the most knowledge about this, says: The narrator named Habib has not heard hadiths from Urwa."
"499","Narrated ``Urwah: Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) used to pray, even though drops of blood were falling on the mat. Similarly, with regard to kissing, the narrator named Yahya has described: \Describe it from me.\"" The status of both of them is the same"
"500","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution and after performing ablution he would kiss (his wife) and then pray and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Waqiyyah has stated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss one of his wives and then perform the prayer and would not perform ablution again. A narrator named Ibn Mahdi has narrated this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss her (his wife) and not perform ablution again. Narrated Abu Asim: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) and then pray and not perform ablution again. The same hadith has been narrated along with some other traditions, but there is some difference in its traditions. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss while fasting. There are these words in a hadith: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss and not perform ablution again, Allah knows best!"
"501","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) after performing ablution and would not perform ablution again. (The narrator doubts, perhaps these are the words:) You used to pray."
"502","It is narrated along with another chain of transmission: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) after performing ablution and then pray."
"503","Ms. Sayyida Hafsa, the wife of the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, narrates this about the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: He used to perform ablution for prayer and then kiss (his wife) and not perform ablution again."
"504","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss her while he was fasting. Uthman bin Abu Sha'ba has narrated in the same way."
"505","Amr bin Shuaib narrates the statement of Sayyidah Zaynab: He asked Sayyidah Aisha Siddiqa (may God be pleased with her) about a person who kisses his wife and touches her. So Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) replied: \Sometimes the Prophet (PBUH) would perform ablution and then kiss me and then go back and pray and would not perform ablution again.\"" The narrator of this tradition is an anonymous narrator named Zainab and such a tradition cannot be presented as evidence."""
"506","Amr Ibn Shuaib narrates this on the authority of Sayyidah Zaynab: Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrated that: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allaah be upon him) used to kiss her and then pray and not perform ablution again. According to Ata, kissing does not require ablution."
"507","This tradition is also narrated along with another document."
"508","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) used to kiss one of his wives and then not perform ablution again. Here the narrator's statement that this hadith is narrated from Abdullah bin Ghalib is an illusion. What they meant was: It was narrated from Ghalib bin Ubaidullah, and this narrator is obsolete."
"509","Ata is convinced: \Kissing does not require ablution.\"""""
"510","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kiss (his wife) while he was fasting, then after that he would perform the prayer and not perform ablution again. It is flawed in several respects."
"511","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA): According to him, kissing does not make ablution necessary."
"512","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \Kissing does not make ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
"513","Sayyidna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with him), she says: Once at night I did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the bed. I am, only You can be helped in Your presence and I cannot praise You and I cannot describe Your praise, Your praise is the same as You yourself have described Your own praise. There are some differences in the authenticity of this tradition."
"514","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Sometimes the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Ghusl Janabat (in the cold season) and I had not yet done Ghusl Janabat."
"515","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: Once I did not find the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on my bed, so I got up. I thought that he had gone to visit his maidservant Maria. They were praying in the state of: \O Allah! I seek refuge in Your forgiveness from Your punishment"
"516","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) says: \Whoever kisses his wife while she is in a state of ablution"
"517","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this: Sayyidna Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said this: \Kissing is part of touching (which is mentioned in the Qur'an)"
"518","Salim narrates this saying of his father (Sayyidna Abdullah bin Umar, may God be pleased with him): He said this about a man kissing and touching his wife with his hand: \This is part of malamast"
"519","Salim narrated this on the authority of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA): He used to think: \Kissing is part of Lams (touching"
"520","Sayyiduna Abdullah Bin Umar Radiyallahu Anhuma said this about kissing: \It makes ablution necessary.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
"521","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) said: \Kissing is a part of 'touching'.\"""""
"522","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"523","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of touch and it becomes necessary to perform ablution on it.\"" Ibn 'Arafah and the narrator Ma'ali have added this: \""Touch is something other than intercourse.\"" And this is authentic."""
"524","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of \""touching\"". This tradition is authentic."""
"525","Sayyiduna Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu says: \Kissing is a part of \""touching\"". This tradition is authentic."""
"526","The same hadith has been narrated in the same way along with some other traditions."
"527","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the privilege of being a companion of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), narrates that: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: \When a person touches his private parts"
"528","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution like the ablution of prayer.\"" This tradition is authentic."""
"529","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the privilege of being a companion of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam), narrates that: The Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: \When a person touches his private parts"
"530","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \Whoever touches his private parts should perform ablution again.\"""""
"531","Nafi', narrates the saying of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with him: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Whoever touches his private parts"
"532","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \When a person moves his hand towards his private area"
"533","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: \When a man touches his private parts"
"534","Amr bin Shuaib narrates the saying of the Prophet, peace be upon him, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather: \Whoever touches his private parts"
"535","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \There is ruin for those who touch their private parts and offer prayers without performing ablution.\"" Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: \""May my parents be sacrificed to you! This ruling is for men"
"536","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever touches his private parts or touches his testicles and touches his pubic area should perform ablution.\"" This tradition has been narrated along with some other traditions"
"537","Sayyidah Basrah bint Sufyan (RA) narrates: She heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Whoever touches his private parts"
"538","Hisham bin Arwah narrates: My father used to say: \When a person touches his private parts or his testicles or his private parts"
"539","Sayyidah Basra bint Sufyan, who had the honor of being the companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person touches his private parts or his testicles"
"540","Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (RA) narrates this statement of his father: I attended the service of the Holy Prophet (PBUH). At that time, people were busy building the mosque of Medina. Narrator narrates: People were moving stones at that time. The narrator narrates: I said, \O Messenger of Allah! Shall I not do the same as these people are moving (stones)?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""No! Rather"
"541","Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this statement from his father: I was with the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he asked him about touching the private parts. A narrator named Ibn Abi Hatim narrates: I asked my father (Abu Hatim) and Sayyiduna Abu Shaykh Zarrah Razi about this tradition narrated by a narrator named Muhammad bin Jabir, and they both replied: \The narrator named Qays bin Talaq is not one to be accepted as authentic.\"" So these two gentlemen showed this narrator to be weak and did not declare him as authentic."""
"542","Abu Uthman Nahdi narrates: Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (RA) narrated this. It is narrated in a hadith: A narrator named Asma bin Malik Hatami, who was a companion of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated this: A person said: \O Messenger of Allah! I got an itch during the prayer. When I itched"
"543","Qays bin Talaq narrates the statement of his father Sayyiduna Talq bin Ali (RA): We set out in a delegation to attend the presence of the Prophet (PBUH), when we entered his presence, we pledged allegiance to him and prayed in his lead. Have an opinion?” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \He is a piece of your body.\"" (The narrator doubts"
"544","Sayyiduna Qays bin Talaq (RA) narrates this on the authority of his father: We asked the Prophet (PBUH) about touching the private parts, and he (PBUH) said: “It is a part of your body.” The narrator of this tradition is Ayyub, unknown."
"545","A Muhaddith named Raja bin Marji narrates: Once we gathered in the mosque of Khaif, among whom were Ahmad bin Hanbal, Ali bin Madini and Yahya bin Mu'in, and a discussion broke out between them about touching the private parts, and Yahya said: \After this"
"546","Shaqiq narrates: Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated: \I do not care if I touch my private parts or touch my nose while I am in the state of prayer.\"""""
"547","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \I do not care whether I touch my private part or touch my ear during prayer.\"""""
"548","Ubaidullah narrates: Sayyiduna Umar was asked about touching the armpit, and he said: \Wudhu will be performed after that.\"""""
"549","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \It will not be necessary for such a person to perform ablution again.\"""""
"550","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him: \It will not be necessary for such a person to perform ablution again.\"""""
"551","Sayyiduna Umar bin Al-Khattab Radiyallahu Anhu says: \When a person touches his armpit"
"552","Hammad bin Zayd has stated this: When Ayub was mentioned about touching the armpits, he said: \Some armpits are like that"
"553","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Wudhu must be performed on what comes out"
"554","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put his back on and prayed and did not perform ablution again, he only washed the part where he put his back on. Ibn Abu Ashreen narrates this tradition as a \marfu'\"" hadith"
"555","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution (washing his face), he would touch his cheeks and stroke his beard downwards with his fingers."
"556","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with him): When he performed ablution, he would touch his two cheeks and sometimes stroke his beard with his fingers, and sometimes leave it off. This tradition is \suspended\"" and rightly so."""
"557","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: When the Prophet (PBUH) performed ablution, he gently touched his cheeks and stroked his beard with his fingers."
"558","Qatadah and Yazid al-Raqashi have narrated this: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to perform ablution, (after this is according to the previous hadith)."
"559","Ismail bin Muhammad al-Safar narrated to us that Ibrahim bin Hani narrated to us, he said that Abu al-Mughira narrated to us, he said that Uza’i narrated to us, he said that Abdul Wahid bin Qays narrated to us, he said that Yazid al-Raqashi narrated this hadith from the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and if this hadith is “Mursal” (meaning the middle narrator is missing), then it is also authentic."
"560","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \When a person has a hemorrhage during his prayer"
"561","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \The water of the sea is the ablution water of the angels. When they descend"
"562","Sayyiduna Ali bin Talaq (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person passes out during prayer"
"563","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person vomits or belches bitterly during prayer"
"564","Ibn Juraj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \When a person vomits or belches sourly during prayer"
"565","This hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa."
"566","This hadith is also narrated along with another document."
"567","Ibn Juraj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever belches or vomits or has a hemorrhage (and this happens during prayer)"
"568","This tradition along with another chain of transmission has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa."
"569","This tradition is narrated from Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) along with another chain of transmission. The same tradition is also transmitted as \Mursal\"" along with another document."""
"570","Ibn Juraj narrates this on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \When a person bleeds or vomits during prayer"
"571","Ibn Jaraj has narrated a similar tradition on the authority of Ibn Abi Malikah, on the authority of Sayyida Ayesha, and on the authority of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"572","Ibn Jurayj narrates the statement of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said this: \When a person vomits during prayer"
"573","Ibn Jaraj, in reference to his father, quotes the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace be upon him: \Whoever has a hemorrhage"
"574","Imam Zayd bin Ali narrates this statement of his grandfather, on the authority of his father: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: \Sour belching or (vomiting) breaks ablution.\"" The narrator of this tradition is Sawar"
"575","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \When a person feels a rumbling in his stomach"
"576","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: \When a person is leading the people in prayer and feels a rumbling in his stomach or he has a hemorrhage or vomits"
"577","Sayyiduna Salman Farsi (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet saw me, blood was flowing from my nose, so he said: \Perform ablution again.\"" A narrator named Mahamali has made this clear: \""It means you perform ablution"
"578","This same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which these words are: \His haemorrhage broke out"
"579","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: If the Prophet (PBUH) had a haemorrhage during the prayer, he (PBUH) would perform ablution and perform the remaining prayer. The narrator of this tradition is ``Amr bin Riyah, obsolete."
"580","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) performed the prayer after ablution and did not perform ablution again. The Prophet (PBUH) only washed the place where he had put his heels."
"581","Sayyiduna Tamim Dari (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \Wudhu becomes necessary after every bleeding.\"" The narrator of this tradition"
"582","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him: \It is not necessary to perform ablution if one or two drops of blood appear"
"583","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \A drop or two drops of blood does not make ablution obligatory"
"584","Sayyiduna Abu Saeed Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever has a hemorrhage during prayer"
"585","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever breaks his ablution"
"586","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \When a person breaks his ablution during prayer"
"587","Sayyida Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates: \When a person breaks his ablution during prayer"
"588","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) has permitted the blood of boils and abscesses (it does not require ablution)."
"589","Sayyida Ayesha Siddiqa (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \Whoever breaks his ablution during prayer should hold his nose and then go back and perform ablution.\"""""
"590","Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) ended his fast by saying this. The narrator narrates: Later, I met Sayyidna Thawban (RA) in the Jamia Masjid of Damascus, I mentioned this to him, and he said (Abu Dardaa said the truth) that I performed ablution on the Prophet (PBUH)."
"591","A narrator named Saad narrated: Sayyiduna Abu Dardaa (RA) narrated this hadith to him, then he narrated a similar hadith from the Prophet (PBUH) on the authority of Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (RA) and on the authority of Sayyidna Thawban (RA)."
"592","Ma'dan bin Abu Talha narrates this: Sayyidna Abu Dardaa (may Allah be pleased with him) told him, after that he mentioned the previous hadeeth, in which it is mentioned: (Sayyidna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) said:) \I performed ablution on the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).\"""""
"593","This tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which there are these words: Sayyidna Thawban (RA) said: \He has said the truth"
"594","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: A person said: \O Messenger of Allah! Whenever I perform ablution (blood) starts flowing.\"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""When you perform ablution"
"595","Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was fasting. It was something other than Ramadan. He suffered something that tormented him, which caused him to vomit. Then he vomited. Then he called me for ablution and performed ablution and ended the fast. I said: \O Messenger of Allah! Is it obligatory to perform ablution after vomiting?\"" The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""If this was a duty"
"596","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) narrates: Once the Prophet (PBUH) fell asleep, he was in a state of prostration at that time, until he started snoring, then he stood up and prayed. I said: \O Messenger of Allah! You were asleep.\"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \""Wudhu is obligatory on a person who sleeps lying down"
"597","Sayyiduna Mu'awiya bin Abu Sufyan (RA) narrates this: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The eye is the closure of the anus"
"598","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"599","Sayyidna Amr bin Shuaib narrates this statement of his grandfather, regarding his father: The Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \Whoever sleeps while sitting"
"600","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abu Talib (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said this: \The eye is a blockage of the anus. Whoever sleeps"
"601","Abu Malih narrates this on the authority of his father: Once we were praying in the company of the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, and a man who was blind came, and we laughed when he fell into the pit, so the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, ordered us to perform complete ablution again and pray anew. The same hadith is narrated along with another chain of transmission, in which both Hasan bin Dinar and Hasan bin Amara are weak narrators, they have made a mistake in its chain of transmission. Hasan al-Basri has narrated this tradition on the authority of Hafsa bint Salman, on the authority of Abul Aaliya. Hasan often cites the \Messenger\"" tradition with reference to the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him). Even Hasan bin Amara has related this tradition"
"602","Abul Malih narrates on the authority of his father: We were praying in the footsteps of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, while a blind man came and fell into the pit, that is, the well in the mosque, so some people behind the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, laughed. The narrator of this hadith is Hasan bin Dinar, the abandoned hadith. This tradition has also been narrated by Abd al-Rahman bin Amr, this narrator is also an abandoned hadith, he has narrated this tradition on the authority of Qatadah, on the authority of Abul Aaliya, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may Allah be pleased with him, on the authority of a narrator named Salam."
"603","Narrated Anas bin Malik: A blind person fell into a well, some people behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again. A narrator named Abu Aamiyyah has narrated this: It was narrated on the authority of Anas (RA): The Prophet (PBUH) was leading the people in prayer, while a blind man entered the mosque, he fell into a well, some people laughed behind the Prophet (PBUH). A narrator named Ibn Mukhlid and Sayyiduna Anas (may God be pleased with him) narrated this on the authority of Abul Aaliyah: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in prayer. There was a well in the middle of the mosque. A narrator named Abu Aamiyyah narrates: This hadith is rejected. Shaykh Abul Hasan says: This hadith has been narrated from a narrator named Salam by a narrator named Abd al-Rahman, this person is a muratuk who compiles hadiths. This tradition has been narrated by Dawud bin Muhibr, this person is also obsolete, who compiles hadiths, he has narrated this tradition from Ayyub's father, who is weak, he has narrated it from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) regarding Qatadah."
"604","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading us in prayer, while a blind man came, he fell into a pit and started crying. This is the correct statement of the person who narrated it as a \Mursal\"" hadith on the authority of Qatadah"
"605","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A blind man fell into a well. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions in prayer. Some of those who were praying under the guidance of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed at this, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again."
"606","Abul Aaliyah narrates this: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions in prayer, while a man fell into the well, some of the people present laughed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed again to perform ablution and pray."
"607","This hadith has been narrated on the authority of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
"608","This hadith is narrated from the Holy Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the authority of Abul Aliya along with another chain of transmission."
"609","This tradition is narrated from Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission."
"610","‘Uthman narrated to us: Ibrahim narrated to us: ‘Ubayd Allah narrated to us: Mu‘tamir narrated to us from Salm—meaning Ibn Abi al-Dhiyal—from Qatadah, who said: It has reached us from the Prophet (ﷺ) similarly. And this is the authentic [narration] from Qatadah; Ma‘mar, Abu ‘Awanah, Sa‘id ibn Abi ‘Arubah, and Sa‘id ibn Bashir agreed upon it, narrating it from Qatadah, from Abu al-‘Aliyah, mursal. And Salm ibn Abi al-Dhiyal followed them in narrating it from Qatadah, mursal. These are five trustworthy narrators who reported it from Qatadah, from Abu al-‘Aliyah, mursal. As for Ayyub ibn Khut, Dawud ibn al-Muhabbar, ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn ‘Amr ibn Jablah, and al-Hasan ibn Dinar—all of them are abandoned (matruk), and none of them is fit to be cited as evidence even if he had no opponent; how much more so when each of them is contradicted by five trustworthy companions of Qatadah? And as for the hadith of al-Hasan ibn Dinar from al-Hasan, from Abu al-Malih, from his father—it is also far from correctness, and we know of no one who followed him upon it. ‘Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah narrated it from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah, but ‘Abd al-Karim is abandoned, and his narrator is ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn al-Husayn, who is also weak. And ‘Umar ibn Qays al-Makki, known as Sindul—who is weak, his hadith rejected—narrated it from ‘Amr ibn ‘Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from ‘Imran ibn Husayn, from the Prophet (ﷺ). As for the hadith of ‘Abd al-Karim… [text cuts off]."
"611","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): \When a person laughs (during the prayer)"
"612","Sayyiduna Imran bin Hussain (RA) narrates: I heard the Prophet (PBUH) saying: \Whoever laughs during the prayer"
"613","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us; Ahmad ibn al-Hasan al-Sufi narrated to us; Sufyan ibn Muhammad narrated to us—and the most favorable assessment of Sufyan ibn Muhammad is that he erred in this hadith—on the authority of Ibn Wahb, if he did not deliberately fabricate it in his statement ""from al-Hasan, from Anas."" For others have narrated it from Ibn Wahb, from Yunus, from al-Zuhri, from al-Hasan, as a mursal (interrupted chain) from the Prophet ﷺ. Among them: Khalid ibn Khidash al-Muhallabi, Mawhib ibn Yazid, and Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb. And others did not mention Anas ibn Malik in their hadith from Ibn Wahb in the chain, nor did they mention Sulayman ibn Arqam between al-Zuhri and al-Hasan, even though he was al-Zuhri's nephew. And Ibn Abi Atiq narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Hasan, as a mursal from the Prophet ﷺ. These are four opinions from al-Hasan, all of them invalid; because al-Hasan only heard this hadith from Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari, from Hafsa bint Sirin, from Abu al-Aliyah al-Riyahi, as a mursal from the Prophet ﷺ."
"614","Sayyiduna Hasan Basri narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, a man with weak eyesight came, (the narrator suspects) that he was blind, he fell into the well, some people laughed, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to pray again and perform ablution. The narrator narrates: I mentioned this tradition to Hafs bin Salman, so he said: \I narrated this tradition to Hasan al-Basri with reference to Hafsa (daughter of Sirin)"
"615","Abu Ali Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Saffar narrated to us (L12530), Isma'il ibn Ishaq al-Qadi (L12383) narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini (L5792) narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi (L4493) said to me: ""This hadith revolves around Abu al-Aliyah."" So I said: ""Al-Hasan has narrated it mursalan (without mentioning the Companion)."" He said: ""Hammad ibn Zayd (L2491) narrated to me, from Hafs ibn Sulayman al-Minqari, he said: 'I narrated it to Al-Hasan, from Hafsah, from Abu al-Aliyah.'"" I said: ""Then Ibrahim has narrated it mursalan."" Abd al-Rahman said: ""Sharik narrated to me, from Abu Hashim, he said: 'I narrated it to Ibrahim, from Abu al-Aliyah.'"" I said: ""Al-Zuhri has narrated it mursalan."" He said: ""I read it in the book of Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from Al-Hasan."""
"616","Hasan bin Abul Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed during the prayer to repeat the prayer and perform ablution again."
"617","Hasan narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, a person came and fell into a well."
"618","Hasan al-Basri narrates: Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, a person came and fell into the well."
"619","Hasan bin Abul Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed during the prayer to perform ablution again and perform the prayer again."
"620","Hasan narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, after that, according to the previous hadith."
"621","Zahri said: Laughing or laughing (during the prayer) does not break Wudhu. What Zahri has quoted from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding Hasan, if it was correct according to Zahri, he would not have issued a fatwa against it and contrary to it, Allah knows best!"
"622","Ma'bad narrates this about the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Once the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, a blind man came, who fell into the pit, and some people laughed, until they laughed. When he finished the prayer, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Whoever among you laughed"
"623","Al-Mabadi Jahani narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the morning prayer, while a blind man came, near the place of the Prophet’s prayer, there was a well, on which a bucket was placed. It has been fixed, he should perform ablution (again) and perform the prayer again."
"624","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was praying. A man with poor eyesight came, passed by a well (pit) with a log lying on it, and fell into the pit. Some of those who were praying behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, finished the prayer and said: \He who laughed among you should perform ablution again and perform the prayer.\"" These words are from a narrator named Ziyad bin Ayyub."""
"625","Ibn Sirin narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the Companions in prayer, after that the hadith was narrated as before, but he narrated these words: When that person fell into the pit, some people laughed behind the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, so the Prophet (peace be upon him) gave this order, after that the hadith was narrated as before. This tradition is authentic, which is narrated on the authority of Khalid on the authority of Hafsa on the authority of Abul Aaliyah. A muhaddith called Hasan says: It is narrated on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abul Malih, on the authority of his father, this is a very clear mistake. The same tradition has been narrated by some other narrators on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
"626","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, while a person came who had poor eyesight and fell into a pit. The people laughed at him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered: Those who laughed should perform ablution again and pray."
"627","This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"628","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading his companions in prayer, while a man came, he placed his foot on the basket, which was placed at the head of the well, and fell into the well. Then the people behind the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laughed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered some of those who laughed: They should perform ablution again and perform the prayer. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"629","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was leading his companions in prayer. There was a blind person among those present, who fell into the well. Some of the companions laughed, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, offered the prayer and ordered those who laughed to perform ablution and pray again. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"630","This same hadith is narrated from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, along with another chain of transmission on the authority of Abul Aaliyah."
"631","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his Companions in prayer. Meanwhile, a man with weak eyesight passed by a pit, on which something was placed, and he fell into the pit. The same tradition is narrated from another hadith."
"632","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions to pray, while a person came who fell into the pit, and some of the people present laughed. This tradition is transmitted along with other evidences."
"633","Abul Aaliyah narrates on the authority of an Ansari: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading his companions to pray, while a person with poor eyesight came and fell into the pit."
"634","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered those who laughed to pray again and perform ablution."
"635","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person came who had weak eyesight, while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, he fell into the pit that was in the mosque, so some people laughed."
"636","This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission."
"637","This same hadith has been narrated from the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the authority of Abul Aaliya along with another chain of transmission."
"638","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person fell into a pit and some of the people who were praying behind the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed."
"639","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the people in the Fajr prayer or in the evening prayer. There was a pit in the mosque. A person with poor eyesight fell into the pit and some people laughed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished the prayer and asked the people the reason for laughing, and they told him the reason."
"640","Abul Aaliyah narrates: Some of those who were praying in the footsteps of the Holy Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) laughed, so the Prophet (Sallallahu Alaihi Wasallam) said: The person who laughed should perform ablution and pray again."
"641","Abul Aaliyah narrates: A person fell into a pit and some of the people who were praying in the footsteps of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed."
"642","Abul Aaliyah narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was leading the prayer, there was a hole in the mosque, a person who was blind came and some people laughed, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered, those who laughed should perform ablution again and perform the prayer."
"643","Ibrahim narrates: A blind man came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying at that time, he slipped and fell into the pit, so the people laughed."
"644","This hadith has been narrated as a \Mursal\"" tradition with reference to Ibrahim"
"645","Asim narrates: Ibn Sirin said to me: Recite the hadith you have to recite! But do not narrate any hadith to me regarding two men from Basra: Abul Aaliyah and Hasan, because these two do not care who they get their hadith from."
"646","Muhammad bin Sirin says: There are four people who authenticate everyone who narrates their hadith and they do not care from whom they have taken the hadith. Hasan Basri, Abul Aliya, Hameed bin Hilal, Dawood bin Abu Hind. This tradition is narrated by Jabir on the authority of Amish, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, he has mentioned this hadith and also mentioned its cause."
"647","Sayyiduna Jabir (RA) narrated: The Prophet (PBUH) said to us: He who laughs during the prayer should perform ablution again and perform the prayer. Shaykh Abu Bakr Neshapuri says: This Hadith is rejected and not authentic. It is authentically narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir to the contrary."
"648","Sayyiduna Jabir says: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary."
"649","Sayyiduna Jabir says: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary."
"650","Sufyan narrates: Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) was asked about a person who laughs during the prayer, (so he said:) He will perform the prayer again, but ablution will not be required for him."
"651","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu says: When a person laughs during the prayer, he will perform the prayer again, but ablution is not required on him."
"652","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: If a person laughs during the prayer, he should repeat the prayer, but it is not necessary to perform ablution on him."
"653","It was narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that: He was asked about laughing during the prayer, and he said: That person will perform the prayer again, but it is not necessary for him to perform ablution."
"654","A narrator named Abu Sufyan has narrated this, Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Radiyallahu Anhu has said this about the one who laughs during the prayer, that person should perform the prayer again, but it is not necessary to perform ablution again. This tradition is narrated from Sha'bi along with another chain of transmission."
"655","A narrator named Abu Sufyan narrates: He heard Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) say: A person who laughs during prayer does not require ablution. This tradition is narrated along with another document."
"656","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary."
"657","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: Laughing (during prayer) does not make ablution necessary (i.e. does not break ablution)."
"658","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates this on the authority of the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “Laughter breaks the prayer, but it does not break the ablution.”"
"659","There is another hadith to the contrary, narrated by Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Talking (during prayer) breaks the prayer"
"660","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) that, according to him, laughing during prayer does not make ablution necessary."
"661","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said: \Smiling does not break the prayer"
"662","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Masoud Radiyallahu Anhu says: When a person laughs during the prayer, it is necessary to perform the prayer again."
"663","Hameed bin Hilal says: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) left with a delegation, in this delegation there was a blind man from the tribe of Abdul Qays. Sayyidna Abu Musa (RA) was leading the prayer. Narrated Ahnaf: When I heard his voice saying that he had fallen into the well, everyone in the audience laughed except me and Sayyiduna Abu Musa Ash'ari. Sayyiduna Abu Musa completed the prayer and inquired: What happened to these people? These people said: So-and-so had fallen into the pit, so Sayyiduna Abu Musa ordered him to pray again."
"664","Hameed bin Hilal narrates: Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari (RA) was teaching his companions to pray, those companions saw something that made them laugh, so Sayyidna Abu Musa Ash'ari, after finishing the prayer, said: Whoever among you laughed should perform the prayer again."
"665","It has been narrated about Sayyiduna Abu Musa Al-Ash'ari (RA): He was leading the people in prayer, and the people saw something at which some people laughed at the example of Sayyidna Abu Musa. After completing the prayer, Sayyiduna Abu Musa (RA) said: \Whoever laughed among you should perform the prayer again.\"""""
"666","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was teaching the Asr prayer to his companions. He smiled during the prayer. Have you smiled during prayer? The narrator narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \Mikael passed by me"
"667","Sahl bin Mu'adh narrates on the authority of his father, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: \The one who laughs"
"668","Sayyiduna Jabir Radiyallahu Anhu says: A person who laughs during the prayer does not need to perform ablution on him. This order was for those who were performing the prayer following the example of the Prophet (peace be upon him)."
"669","Sayyiduna Hudhayfah (RA) narrates: The Prophet (PBUH) said: \The entire surface of the earth has been made a place for us to pray"
"670","The same tradition is narrated along with another chain of transmission, which reads: \All the earth has been made for us a place of prayer and a means of purification when we cannot find water.\"""""
"671","Umayr, who was the slave of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, says: Once, I and Abdullah bin Yasar, who is the slave of Sayyida Maimunah, the wife of the Holy Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, both of us attended the service of Sayyidna Abu Jaham bin Harith Ansari, and Sayyidna Abu Jaham, may God be pleased with him, said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was coming from the well of Jamal. Aya, he greeted you, the Prophet did not respond to the greeting. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approached the wall, wiped his face and both arms (i.e. performed tayammum) and then greeted it."
"672","Sayyiduna Abu Jaham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was going to the well of Jamal to relieve himself. He met a man who was coming from the front."
"673","Sayyiduna Abu Jaham bin Harith (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Once the Holy Prophet (peace be upon him) was going to the well of Jamal to relieve himself. A person greeted him from the front, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not respond to the greeting, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his blessed hand on the wall and wiped his blessed face and both arms with it (i.e. performed tayammum), then he said: “Peace be upon you too.”"
"674","Sayyiduna Abu Jaham (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was coming to the well of the camel, perhaps after defecating or urinating. I greeted you, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not respond to my greeting, then the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned his hand on the blessed wall and wiped his blessed face and both arms with it (i.e. performed tayammum), then he responded to my greeting."
"675","The same hadith along with another chain of transmission is narrated on the authority of Sayyidina Abu Jaham (RA) about the Holy Prophet (PBUH)."
"676","Narrated by Nafi: Once, I attended the service of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace, in connection with some work of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may God bless him and grant him peace. The Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was visiting after defecating or urinating. This person greeted him, the Prophet (peace be upon him) did not respond to him, until the person was about to leave the street, when the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned his hands on the blessed wall and wiped his face, then turned again and wiped both his arms (i.e. performed tayammum), then he responded to his greeting. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: \I did not respond to you because I was not in a state of ablution.\"""""
"677","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (RA) narrates this: Once the Prophet (PBUH) was coming home after defecating. A man came to him near the well of Jamal, he greeted him, the Prophet did not return his greeting until he came to the wall and wiped his face and both arms (i.e. performed tayammum) then returned the man's greeting."
"678","Saeed bin Jubayr narrates: Sayyidna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said this about Allah's commandment: \If you are sick or on a journey.\"" Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \""When a person gets a wound in the way of Allah"
"679","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (RA) says: \It is permissible for a sick person to perform tayammum through clay.\"""""
"680","Ata narrated this tradition as a marfu', hadith, up to the Prophet, may God's prayers and peace be upon him, while other narrators narrated it as a muwaqf tradition."
"681","Sayyiduna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: Once I had a fever in a winter night, it was a matter of Ghazwa Zaat-ul-Salsil, I was afraid that if I bathed, I would be killed, so I performed Tayammum and led the morning prayer to my companions. Later, when this was mentioned to the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he inquired: \O Amr! Did you lead your companions in prayer while you were in Janabat?\"" So I told you about the reason that prevented me from taking bath. I said: I heard Allah saying: \""Do not kill yourselves"
"682","Abu Qais, who is the slave of Sayyidna Amr bin As, narrates: Once Sayyidna Amr bin As, may Allah be pleased with him, went to a house. During this time they had to pack for the cold, it had never been so cold before. When he started to go for the morning prayer, he said: \By Allah! I had a cold last night. Such cold"
"683","Rabi bin Badr narrates this statement of his grandfather regarding his father: Sayyiduna Asla said: \You show me how the Holy Prophet"
